    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/wsu-libraries-student-assistant-access-services-wichita-kansas-united-states-dd4270e9-f335-4c04-b204-aec7719d3097": {
      "title": "WSU Libraries Student Assistant – Access Services",
      "description": "WSU Libraries Student Assistant – Access Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States WSU Libraries Student Assistant – Access Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode WSU Libraries Student Assistant – Access Services Library | Student WSU Libraries Student Assistant – Access Services 499883 Student Department WSU Libraries Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $10/hr Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. up to 20 hours a week depending on availability. • Flexible schedule. Can include evenings, weekends and some daytime. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Circulation • Checking library materials in and out, renewing them and placing holds on them • Answering basic questions about the library, its policies and services, and campus directions • Assisting library users with room bookings, locating items, etc. Interlibrary Loan • Retrieving materials from the stacks and packaging them for shipping for Interlibrary Loan • Scan print articles and chapters on overhead book scanner and deliver electronically to patrons Stacks • Searching for lost/missing library materials • Responsible for service, maintenance, and knowledge of WSU Library stacks • Assists with inventory control of the physical collection to include performing maintenance within the stacks All Areas • Demonstrating basic customer service skills • Gathering statistics for projects as requested by the staff • Must become adept with office equipment, including copier, scanner, and computer • Become familiar with our library catalog and journal databases • Other duties as assigned. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements • Morning (preferably 7am - 1pm) and weekend availability • Enrolled at WSU • Good communication skills • Able to follow written and oral instructions • Basic computer skills • Duties include: squatting, bending, lifting between 5 and 50 pounds, and other physical work Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications • Customer service experience • Library experience Additional Information Work study students are encouraged to apply. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) c5db8952 Last Name (required) f0b58759 Email (required) c261114e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) aca16688 Last Name (required) d3aa4714 Email (required) ccbe3925 Job Alert f3796c14 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your