    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/student-assistant-student-adminstrative-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Student Assistant/Student Adminstrative Assistant",
      "description": "Student Assistant/Student Adminstrative Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Student Assistant/Student Adminstrative Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Student Assistant/Student Adminstrative Assistant Strategic Engagement & Planning | Student Student Assistant/Student Adminstrative Assistant 499850 Student Department TRIO STEM SSS Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $17/hour, 20 hours/week Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Flexible, 20 hours weekly, Mon-Friday 8am-5pm Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The TRIO SSS STEM Program is seeking a detail-oriented and organized student to serve as a Student Administrative Assistant. This position will play an important role in supporting program operations and helping develop administrative processes for a growing federally funded student success program serving STEM majors. This position is ideal for a student interested in organizational leadership, business administration, project management, communications, higher education, nonprofit management, or related fields who would like practical experience supporting program operations and student services. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Support participant outreach and communication efforts Maintain program records and assist with data entry Help develop and document administrative procedures and workflows Assist with participant tracking and attendance management Support office organization and process improvement initiatives Create and update forms, checklists, templates, and other administrative resources Complete general administrative tasks as assigned Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements Currently enrolled as a Wichita State University undergraduate or graduate student. Maintain good academic standing with the university. Demonstrate strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to communicate effectively in writing and verbally. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, Outlook, and Teams. Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines while working independently. Ability to maintain confidentiality when handling student records and information. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications Major or coursework in Business Administration, Organizational Leadership, Project Management, Communication, Marketing, Public Administration, or a related field. Previous experience working in an office, administrative, customer service, student employment, or leadership role. Experience maintaining records, managing data, or supporting organizational processes. Familiarity with Microsoft Forms, Excel, Canva, or other organizational and communication tools. Interest in higher education administration, student success, project management, or program operations. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) ea9ee099 Last Name (required) 6ba3b93b Email (required) 7bda70bd Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscri