    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/hr-assistant-shared-services-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "HR Assistant - Shared Services",
      "description": "HR Assistant - Shared Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States HR Assistant - Shared Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode HR Assistant - Shared Services Culture and HR | Staff HR Assistant - Shared Services 499812 Staff Department: Human Resources Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Beginning at $17.73/hr, adjustment dependent upon qualifications Work Schedule: General business hours (typical M-F 8-5); work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Making an impact happens in this position in so many ways and with so many people! Our team focuses on providing detailed and accurate service to our university partners in all aspects related to hiring, onboarding & after hire updates. This makes this position dedicated to customer service and problem resolution to solution focused. Downstream effects of our work impact multiple systems and partners. We seek an individual who can identify errors others miss & ensure the team is being as accurate, effective & efficient as possible. Your day can change from standard daily tasks to switching gears into problem solving mode or address customer concerns in an instant & then end with an appointment with an employee. The ability to move seamlessly from task to task when interruptions happen, but you are not rattled by this in order to be successful. Recovery from interruptions and regaining focus for attention to detail is a must. This position also provides you with variety in your day, as well as perpetual learning opportunities in the realm of HR. Join the team who helps new employees get started on the right foot, transitions across the university, departments seeking us out for guidance, & depend on us to ensure compliance with all employment aspects at the university! Job Summary Assists with day-to-day operations of human resources functions within a shared services framework. Essential Functions • Provides support to staff in various functional areas by assisting with administering, monitoring, and coordinating programs and processes. • Provides information and assistance to employees by ensuring effective communication and prompt resolution of requests and questions. • Collects, compiles, enters, and verifies data for payroll and employee records. Reviews and verifies incoming and outgoing documentation for completeness, accuracy and compliance. • Assists with the development, planning and implementation of meetings and events which may include scheduling space, room set-up, follow up with customers, and preparing materials, as needed. Job Duties Actively engage department(s) regarding the formal hiring processes and practices at the university, ensuring they fall within compliance &/or policy guidelines. Review of documentation, providing guidance within system operations & university practices. Carries out the daily operations of core HR functions, supporting the hiring processes and after hire transitions. Examples include: running background checks, form completion, storage of documentation, performing I-9 appointments, audit of employee information, & cross checking of info provided by depts pertinent to university processes. Ensures confidentiality and compliance with institutional policies and other regulations governing HR. Reviews, collects and validates data from systems, forms, or other sources to ensure accuracy. Conducting yourself as a professional, ethical, & trustworthy member of HR for the university. Develops training materials, guides, or reference documents for internal needs or the university at large. Triages questions and issues, determining when escalation or referral to another HR member is appropriate. Provide options to stakeholders/depts to operate within, steering them to the appropriate course of action for their needs; OR if not possible, providing them context as to why they cannot proceed. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Six (6) months of experience in human resources, office administration, or related field. Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Provide customer service and communicate clearly both in verbal and written format. Communicate with clear, concise messages while asking deciphering & investigative questions to fully understand situation or scenarios faced with regularly. Ability to multi-task, including stopping and starting tasks to respond to needs. Organized in working through tasks, which may be interrupted, with the ability to pick up where you left off to meet deadlines. Recognize when data and processes appear different and understand the context the work has in a larger process. Understanding of the importance of details, why they need to be cross checked & ensure accuracy in all aspects of work. Take initiative and present solutions that meet compliance, policies & process gaps, if they exist. Basic knowledge related to overall HR guidelines, practices, concepts or laws. Preferred Qualifications: Experience within Human Resources field &/or direct application of common work in HR. Experience in higher education payroll, HR. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 1d5caead Last Name (required) 005fe1b8 Email (required) e5e7ff56 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (whe