    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/student-assistant-work-study-ece-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Student Assistant - Work Study ECE",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Work Study ECE - Wichita, Kansas, United States Student Assistant - Work Study ECE - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Student Assistant - Work Study ECE College of Engineering | Student Student Assistant - Work Study ECE 499856 Student Department Electrical and Computer Engineering Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15.00/hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Office is open 8-5 Monday-Friday. Schedule will vary depending on student's class schedule. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The College of Engineering is seeking a reliable and professional Work-Study Student Assistant to provide front office support and assist with daily administrative operations. This role serves as a key point of contact for visitors, students, faculty, and staff. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Answer and direct incoming phone calls in a courteous and professional manner • Warmly welcome and assist visitors; check in guests and notify appropriate staff of arrivals • Respond to general inquiries and provide basic information about the college • Sort and distribute incoming mail to faculty and staff • Monitor and restock office supplies as needed • Help maintain a clean, organized, and welcoming office environment • Provide administrative support and assist with special projects as assigned Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements • Must be eligible for Federal Work-Study • Minimum GPA of 2.5 • Availability to work 10–15 hours per week between Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–5:00 PM • Strong communication and customer service skills • Dependable, detail-oriented, and able to work both independently and as part of a team • Self-motivated with a strong work ethic and initiative • Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize effectively • Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite; willingness to learn new systems • Prior phone or office experience is helpful; training will be provided Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Additional Information Selection will be based on work-study eligibility, schedule availability, and the ability to follow application instructions. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 3a02765b Last Name (required) 4e2603c4 Email (required) c6e0c068 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 2564b758 Last Name (required) c1bf64d2 Email (required) 562f5933 Job Alert 0f508f89 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages relate