    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-educator-american-sign-language-program-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Educator, American Sign Language Program",
      "description": "Assistant Educator, American Sign Language Program - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Educator, American Sign Language Program - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Educator, American Sign Language Program College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Educator, American Sign Language Program 499617 On Site Faculty Department: American Sign Language Program Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $ 50,000-$55,000 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, times variable dependent on class schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Modern & Classical Languages & Literatures (MCLL) at Wichita State University seeks a passionate and student-centered educator to join its American Sign Language program as an Assistant Educator of American Sign Language with a focus on Interpreter Education. This is a 9-month, non-tenure track faculty appointment beginning August 2, 2027. This position offers the opportunity to foster a new generation of ASL interpreters while contributing to a growing and collaborative language department that values applied learning, community engagement, and service. The successful candidate will help strengthen connections between the university, the Deaf community, and professional interpreting environments while fostering student success through innovative teaching and mentorship. Success in this role means that students graduate with stronger ASL fluency, basic/foundational interpreting skills, and meaningful connections to the Deaf community. Through collaborative teaching, mentorship, and service, you will help advance interpreter education while contributing to a vibrant academic environment and the greater Wichita community. The Department of Modern & Classical Languages & Literatures offers majors in French, Spanish, and American Sign Language, along with minors in French, Spanish, American Sign Language, Japanese, and German. Faculty engage in diverse areas of scholarship and practice, and Wichita State is recognized for its commitment to applied learning and meaningful partnerships with industry and community organizations. This position provides the opportunity to make a lasting impact on students, contribute to the advancement of interpreter education, and engage in service both on campus and throughout the Wichita community. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teach undergraduate American Sign Language and interpreter education courses through a variety of instructional modalities. Create engaging learning experiences that integrate applied learning, experiential projects, and industry-relevant practices. Collaborate with ASL faculty on curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous improvement initiatives. Mentor and advise students as they pursue academic, professional, and career goals in interpreting and Deaf community engagement. Build and maintain relationships with local Deaf community organizations and stakeholders to support student learning and language access initiatives. Participate in outreach activities that enhance community engagement and promote the ASL program. Contribute service to the department, college, university, and the broader ASL and interpreting professions. Support Wichita State University's commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration and community-connected learning. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree or Equivalent Experience in the Field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements MA degree in American Sign Language, Interpreting, or related field by start date. Fluency in American Sign Language as demonstrated by test scores or credentials such as but not limited to: ASLPI score of 4 or higher, SLPI rating of Advanced Plus or higher, BEI Advanced Certification, RID certification (NIC or CDI). Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Effective written communication skills. Ability to develop and collaborate in a robust teaching program. Ability to collaborate with diverse academic and non-academic groups. Effective mentoring skills. Demonstrated teaching effectiveness Preferred Qualifications: ASL Interpreting degree Interdisciplinary/industry collaboration experience as demonstrated by professional credentials in the ASL Interpreting profession (either state or national level). Demonstrated instructional effectiveness in teaching interpreting and ASL related content at the college level. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Teaching Statement, including any (including examples of teaching experience i.e. workshops, courses taught, etc., and teaching evaluations if possible) Review of applications will start on December 15th and will continue until the position has been filled . Letters of recommendation will be requested to semifinalists. Feel free to contact Dr. Edward Bart Edward.bart@wichita.edu or Dr. Rocio del Aguila rocio.delaguila@wichita.edu for any questions. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) e1ebbbf7 Last Name (required) e819695f Email (required) 96e3e44f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) bdfeded3 Last Name (required) 24ce2551 Email (required) 3a64a7e5 Job Alert f2d934dc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) f8740fb6 Last Name (required) 24a04240 Email (required) 9dcb02a6 Send This Job To: 938469b9 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" – Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant – Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 38179329 Last Name (required) b78e9b5c Email (required) 5f312fa8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any tim