    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-clinical-psychology-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology 499795 On Site Faculty Department: Department of Psychology Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $70,000.00 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8am to 5pm; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Psychology Department at Wichita State University seeks to hire a 9-month tenure-track, Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology to begin August 2, 2027. We welcome applications from individuals with a cognitive-behavioral orientation as broadly-defined. We are open to all areas of research and clinical interests, but are especially interested in scholars who could contribute in one or more of the following areas: integrated behavioral healthcare in the primary care setting, family systems approaches, and third-wave behavioral therapies. Applicants should be PhD graduates of an APA- accredited program in clinical psychology, (completed prior to August of 2027), licensed (or licensed-eligible) as a psychologist in the state of Kansas, and have a strong record of peer-reviewed publications. The Clinical Psychology PhD Program at Wichita State is fully-accredited by the American Psychological Association and embraces a scientist–practitioner model, within a clinical–community framework. The department has three Ph.D. programs in clinical, community, and human factors psychology, as well as a large undergraduate student body. The department is research oriented and has an expectation for faculty to seek external funding. Wichita State also has an in-house clinical psychology training clinic that serves the greater Wichita area. Salary is $70,000.00. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels, mentor Ph.D. students, conduct research, apply for grants, publish in peer reviewed journals. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD graduate of an APA- accredited program in clinical psychology. Degree should be completed prior to August of 2027. Experience publishing in peer-reviewed journals Required License/Certifications/Training: Licensed (or licensed-eligible) as a psychologist in the state of Kansas. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Training in clinical psychology Ability to contribute to building an inclusive and welcoming environment for colleagues and students Ability to work effectively in a highly collaborative, engaging, and dynamic environment comprised of individuals with a range of backgrounds, skills, and perspectives. Ability to attract external funding Commitment to teach both graduate and undergraduate courses Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research philosophy Description of how you work to create a cooperative and welcoming work place. (attach as Faculty Document 1) Review of applications will begin November 20, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For questions, please contact Samantha Slade at samantha.slade@wichita.edu WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) d6dc725f Last Name (required) 71dc2751 Email (required) 0b856bb1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 568dbd71 Last Name (required) 54c0f283 Email (required) 4461e1f5 Job Alert f4a363be Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 7f77eb34 Last Name (required) f090fe1d Email (required) 06782ad3 Send This Job To: 8ac57d08 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" – Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant – Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (r