    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/administrative-specialist-forensic-programs-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist, Forensic Programs",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist, Forensic Programs - Wichita, Kansas, United States Administrative Specialist, Forensic Programs - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Administrative Specialist, Forensic Programs College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Staff Administrative Specialist, Forensic Programs 499610 Staff Department: School of Criminal Justice Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range begins at $17.73 and is commensurate with experience Work Schedule: 8-5, M-F; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The School of Criminal Justice has an exciting opportunity for an Administrative Specialist who will play a pivotal role in the smooth operation of the new Master's of Forensic Biology and Master's of Forensic Firearms programs. Supporting these new programs will involve juggling room bookings, managing budgets, advising students on non-academic matters and ensuring all administrative tasks are handled with precision and care. We are looking for someone with a friendly nature and proactive approach to be an indispensable member of the team as we work to support the mission of providing top-notch education in criminal justice. Job Summary Performs a variety of professional and administrative duties that facilitate the operations of a function(s), program(s), and/or department(s). Essential Functions Supports the programs and services provided by the department(s) by performing varied or related processes which may include creating and maintaining databases and websites, monitoring, facilitating, and enforcing compliance with established criteria, guidelines and standards, etc. May coordinate, attend, prepare materials for and/or take minutes at meetings and special events. May prepare or assist in the preparation of budgets, grant applications, proposals, status reports and/or financial statements. May identify and pursue ways to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of administrative procedures used by students, faculty, visitors and staff. May order and maintain sufficient inventory of office supplies and equipment. May be assigned to lead, assist, coordinate or support special projects as needed. Job Duties Supports the programs and services provided by the School of Criminal Justice by performing varied or related processes which may include creating and maintaining databases and websites, monitoring, facilitating, and enforcing compliance with established criteria, guidelines and standards, etc. Participates in accreditation-related activities. Coordinates, attends, prepares materials for and/or takes minutes at meetings and special events. Plans and coordinates marketing and Forensic Science recruiting events. Coordinates accreditation-related activities, including data collection and document control. Prepares or assists in the preparation of budgets, grant applications, proposals, status reports and/or financial statements. Organizes admissions materials and processes for the Admissions Committee. Maintains written marketing materials by organizing inventories, placing orders, tracking usage, and ensuring materials are available for recruitment and outreach activities. Responds to information requests. Orders and maintains sufficient inventory of lab /office supplies and equipment. Identifies and pursues ways to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of administrative procedures used by students, faculty, visitors and staff. May be assigned to lead, assist, coordinate or support special projects as needed. Other duties as assigned. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Two (2) years of experience in general office, clerical, administrative support or related field Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, specifically Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Teams; and in record keeping. Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize activity to ensure deadlines are met. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Excellent attention to detail Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information with discretion Ability to work collaboratively in a professional office environment Demonstrated ability to work with frequent interruptions and changing priorities Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree Experience with marketing, event planning and social media platforms Knowledge of university infrastructure, policies, and procedures Knowledge of university platforms, e,g, Banner, BlackBoard, Slate Demonstrated ability to solve operational problems and make suggestions for process improvement Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Sedentary: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Sedentary work involves remaining stationary most of the time. Apply Now First Name (required) f9a890c5 Last Name (required) 6a28e91d Email (required) a2a6aeb2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4f351a50 Last Name (required) 1015b8e7 Email (required) 79cd292d Job Alert d0720882 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown 