    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/parking-enforcement-specialist-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Parking Enforcement Specialist",
      "description": "Parking Enforcement Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States Parking Enforcement Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Parking Enforcement Specialist WSU Police Department | Staff Parking Enforcement Specialist 499715 Staff Department: Parking & Transportation Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range begins at $15.34/hour and is commensurate with experience Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 7 AM - 3 PM; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The University's Parking & Transportation Services has an opening for a 1st shift Parking Enforcement Specialist. This position also comes with a robust benefits package (effective on your first day) and generous paid time off. Job Summary Performs parking compliance work, safeguarding property owned or leased by the University by monitoring and patrolling parking areas for violations and escorting or transporting individuals to specific locations. Essential Functions • Conducts daily monitoring of parking lots for parking violations and issuing parking citations. • Assists in set up and tear down of parking lot reservations and special event needs. Set up and move cones, barricades, parking signs, and VMS (Variable Message Sign) trailers, as needed. • Patrol assigned areas, respond to motorist assistance situations, and observe and report special hazards. • Perform simple vehicle maintenance procedures and report mechanical problems to leadership. Job Duties Provides mobility assistance rides for students, faculty and staff on campus as needed. Assists UPD in performing traffic control duties. Calls upon University police officers to assist with police-related tasks/functions, as necessary. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent None Required License/Certifications/Training: Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) and National Crime Information Center (NCIC) certification within six (6) months of hire date. Valid drivers license Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to efficiently operate the T2 Flex system. Ability to operate a two-way radio. Ability to remain calm under stressful situations. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Ability to give and follow instructions verbally and in writing. Ability to recall and record information concisely and accurately. Ability to read and understand written department guidelines, university policies, laws, rules, and regulations. Ability to build and sustain effective professional and courteous interpersonal relationships with a diverse constituency of faculty, staff, students, and public. Additional Information: During the application process your background will be closely examined. Please review the following background “disqualifiers.” If you think that any of these apply to you and you have questions, please call Parking Services at (316) 978- 5526 for clarification, or for more information. Must not have been convicted of, plead guilty or no contest to, or been diverted on a serious traffic violation within the past three years of date of application. Serious traffic violations to include, but not limited to vehicular homicide, DUI, reckless driving, hit and run, and eluding a police officer. Must not have received three moving violations during the last twelve months or been involved in two accidents for which they were at fault during the past twelve months. Must not be currently charged with, under indictment, or on probation for any criminal activity other than minor traffic violations. Physical Requirements: Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Frequent 60-90% Ability to remain in a stationary position. Occasional 30-60% Ability to inspect and/or surveil materials, equipment, reports, and/or incidents and identify any errors, needs and/or determining factors. Occasional 30-60% Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Occasional 30-60% Ability to drive state vehicle. Occasional 30-60% Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Occasional 30-60% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Rare 0-30% Ability to position self to perform safety and security actions determined by police methods and procedures. Rare 0-30% Ability to move or traverse across campus, within buildings and offices, and/or across external environments. Rare 0-30% Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) ed7f961a Last Name (required) d0b2f9c3 Email (required) 4ee08d60 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 284bb9e9 Last Name (required) 9a41d345 Email (required) 0bb61053 Job Alert e985bf0a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) WSU Police Department WSU Police Department Send Please wait... 