    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/business-technology-analyst-wichita-kansas-united-states-7fb255e2-b9fd-4d86-bee9-2d867f75d02a": {
      "title": "Business Technology Analyst",
      "description": "Business Technology Analyst - Wichita, Kansas, United States Business Technology Analyst - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Business Technology Analyst Financial Operations | Finance, Staff Business Technology Analyst 499506 Finance Staff Department: Financial Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range from $65,700 - $85,000/yr; determined based on qualifications Work Schedule: Hybrid & flexible schedule with core business hours of 8a -5p, Monday-Friday; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Do you enjoy solving complex problems, improving business processes, and helping organizations leverage technology to work smarter? Wichita State University's Financial Services team is seeking talented professionals who brings together technology expertise and financial knowledge to support critical university operations. In this role, you'll work at the intersection of finance, technology, research administration, and customer service. You'll collaborate with stakeholders across campus to support enterprise financial systems, improve business processes, develop reporting solutions, and implement technology enhancements that directly impact faculty, staff, and researchers. You'll participate in strategic initiatives focused on modernization, automation, service excellence, and continuous improvement while helping shape the future of financial operations at Wichita State University. This position offers the opportunity to work with a diverse technology portfolio including Banner Finance, TouchNet, reporting tools, research administration systems, and other enterprise applications. We're looking for curious, analytical professionals who enjoy understanding how systems work, asking questions, solving problems, and creating solutions that make a meaningful difference. If you're passionate about technology, data, accounting, and continuous improvement, we'd love to hear from you. Job Summary Provides analysis and support of software and processes within the assigned functional area which may include, but is not limited to configuration, testing, documentation, support, maintenance and training for solutions, and working closely with business users, leaders, and technical users throughout the lifecycle of a system and/or project. Essential Functions Provides development, analysis and support for systems. Works closely with business users and managers to refine, develop and prioritize business goals and process enhancements. Provides system support, including implementation, testing, training, new releases, and vendor coordination. Works closely with business users and managers to understand, refine and prioritize business goals and information needs. Manages and supports applications, including support, upgrades and troubleshooting May provide support for interfaces. Job Duties Develop a comprehensive understanding of Accounts Receivable, Accounting, and Research Accounting business processes, financial transactions, internal controls, and reporting requirements to serve as a trusted business systems partner. Collaborate with functional users to analyze business needs, troubleshoot complex system and data issues, identify root causes, and recommend solutions that align with accounting principles, regulatory requirements, and university business processes. Serve as the primary liaison between Financial Services stakeholders and technical teams, translating business requirements into functional specifications and ensuring successful implementation of system enhancements and process improvements. Gather reporting requirements from business users and develop, test, and validate SQL queries to support operational, financial, compliance, and management reporting needs. Act as the subject matter expert for financial data structures and reporting logic, partnering with the Cognos reporting team to design, test, validate, and deploy accurate and meaningful reports and dashboards. Support enterprise financial applications through system testing, upgrades, integrations, documentation, training, and continuous improvement initiatives that enhance efficiency, standardization, data integrity, and customer service. Required Education and Experience: 60 hours of college coursework in related field Two (2) years of experience in technology application support or related field Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to analyze business processes, identify issues, and recommend solutions that improve efficiency, accuracy, and internal controls. Knowledge of accounting principles, financial transactions, and ERP systems such as Banner or similar enterprise applications. Ability to gather reporting requirements, analyze data, and validate reporting results. Familiar with writing, testing, and troubleshooting SQL queries used for reporting, reconciliation, and data analysis. Knowledge to investigate and resolve complex system, data, and process-related issues. Ability to gather and document business requirements and effectively communicate technical solutions to functional users and technical teams. Preferred Qualifications: Coursework in accounting, finance, database management, business analysis, or information systems. Experience with Banner Finance, Banner Accounts Receivable, or a comparable ERP system. Experience supporting Accounts Receivable, Accounting, Research Accounting, grants administration, or other financial operations. Experience working with TouchNet, Cognos, Evisions, or similar enterprise applications. Experience working in higher education, state government, or public sector environments. Experience serving as a liaison between business users and technical teams to develop reporting solutions, troubleshoot issues, and improve business processes. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 163b6aad Last Name (required) ffa76c2e Email (required) 9f6a8e37 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 14237d3f Last Name (required) 354784c7 Email (required) 886e1743 Job Alert fdac6edb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Finance Staff Finance Staff Department(s) Financial Operations Financial Operations Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 5b8f4ae6 Last Name (required) 50d8720f Email (required) 5bd1d79b Send This Job To: ebe57fd9 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone num