    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/student-assistant-trio-sss-wichita-kansas-united-states-03848b3c-2103-46d5-ac5c-fcf0e2be7230": {
      "title": "Student Assistant TRIO SSS",
      "description": "Student Assistant TRIO SSS - Wichita, Kansas, United States Student Assistant TRIO SSS - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Student Assistant TRIO SSS Strategic Engagement & Planning | Student Student Assistant TRIO SSS 499766 Student Department TRIO Student Support Services Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $11.00/hr Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Dependent upon student's class schedule and TRIO SSS office hours. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Are you looking for a job where you can make a difference on campus while building your professional skills? TRIO Student Support Services is looking for a friendly and motivated Student Assistant to join our team! As the first point of contact for our office, you'll help create a welcoming environment for students by greeting visitors, answering phones, and assisting with various office tasks. Your role will be essential in supporting the success of TRIO students — many of whom are first-generation college students or come from underrepresented backgrounds. If you’re organized, detail-oriented, a great communicator who enjoys helping others, and ready to make a positive impact, we’d love to have you on board! Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties 1. Perform receptionist duties for the program including: answering the telephone, responding to emails, forwarding messages, attending to program participants & visitors, updating spreadsheets, and scheduling/confirming appointments by making phone calls. 2. Perform clerical work including: Typing, filing, computer data entry, picking up the mail, keeping office supply inventory, cleaning/organizing supplies, setting up/attending SSS events and tablings, and running other daily errands. 3. Maintain confidentiality of information when filing documents in students’ files. 4. Attend training sessions required by the program. 5. Maintain accurate records of time worked in the office. 6. Follow program policies and procedures. 7. Complete work as assigned by program staff members and have excellent communication regarding assigned tasks and prioritizing, as needed. 8. Perform any additional duties as assigned by the Program Director. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements Minimum Requirements: - Enrolled as a sophomore, junior, senior or graduate student at WSU - In Good Academic standing - Have a cumulative 2.5 GPA or better Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications 1. Ability to perform clerical work 2. Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite, Adobe Suite and other graphic software 3. Good customer service skills 4. Ability to organize, prioritize and work on multiple tasks simultaneously 5. Ability to complete tasks in a timely manner with minimal supervision 6. Ability to pay attention to detail 7. Strong verbal and written communication skills 8. Ability to keep records and maintain confidentiality 9. Experience working with students similar to those served by SSS 10. Good judgment and decision-making skills 11. Good analytical and problem-solving skills 12. Ability and willingness to work flexible hours Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) be6a6ba5 Last Name (required) 76c09765 Email (required) dc13abac Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4fbeb4d0 Last Name (required) 7490f578 Email (required) 5e03985d Job Alert e79abc08 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) e38a8849 Last Name (required) a574fd37 Email (required) 4c879612 Send This Job To: 9bbdad20 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" – Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant – Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) fac17a3d Last Name (required) b624c4d4 Email (required) d801fa34 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on