    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-atlas-programming-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR ATLAS Programming Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR ATLAS Programming Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR ATLAS Programming Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR ATLAS Programming Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR ATLAS Programming Student Assistant 497107 Student Department NIAR Advanced Technologies Lab Aerospace Systems (ATLAS) Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15-$18 per hour Work Schedule Based on Class Schedule. Ability to work minimum of 20 hours per week. Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Coding and Development: Writing and testing code for web applications using languages like HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and frameworks like React or Angular. Desktop Application Development: Designing, developing, and maintaining desktop applications using technologies such as .NET (WPF, WinForms), Electron. Performance Optimization: Enhancing the performance and responsiveness of desktop applications by implementing efficient algorithms, reducing memory usage, and optimizing UI rendering. UI/UX Implementation: Creating user-friendly interfaces for desktop applications, ensuring a seamless and intuitive user experience. Database Management: Integrating and managing local or remote databases, such as SQL Server, SQLite, or PostgreSQL, for desktop applications, ensuring efficient data storage and retrieval. User Testing and Feedback Integration: Assisting in user testing to gather feedback on the application's performance, usability, and accessibility, and implementing necessary improvements. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Requirements Proficiency writing and testing code in languages like HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and frameworks like React or Angular. Minimum 20 hours per week Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 6936fd37 Last Name (required) 0baabbdb Email (required) 7f72438a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 301e8cfc Last Name (required) bebe240b Email (required) ed4715ff Job Alert 14ad5eb3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 8e84c4ff Last Name (required) f925f216 Email (required) ce3e6b2e Send This Job T