    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-criminal-justice-homeland-security-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Homeland Security",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Homeland Security - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Homeland Security - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Homeland Security College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Homeland Security 499466 On Site Faculty Department: School of Criminal Justice Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $65,000 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, may vary depending on class schedule; work is performed on-site and in person Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The School of Criminal Justice (SCJ) at Wichita State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position starting on August 2, 2027 in Criminal Justice with the ability to teach and conduct research focused on enforcement issues for professions within Homeland Security. We seek a dynamic and innovative scholar committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The successful candidate will contribute to our undergraduate and graduate programs, engage in impactful research, and participate in departmental, college, and university committees. The salary for this 9-month position will be $65,000. As one of the oldest criminal justice programs in the United States, our school offers bachelor's and master's degrees in Criminal Justice, a fully online bachelor's degree in Homeland Security , a bachelor's degree in Forensic Science, and master’s degrees in Forensic Biology and Forensic Firearms. Due to the school's strong partnership with local and state agencies, faculty have abundant research opportunities. The SCJ is housed in the Law Enforcement Training Center on WSU’s Innovation Campus – a partnership building shared with the Wichita Police Department and the Sedgwick County Sheriff’s Office. The SCJ has close partnerships with the Midwest Criminal Justice Institute and with the US Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms, and Explosives (ATF), which has two buildings on the Innovation Campus housing the Crime Gun Intelligence Center of Excellence, the NIBIN National Correlation and Training Center II, and the ATF Wichita Field Office. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in homeland security. The standard teaching load for research-active faculty is three classes per semester. Develop and maintain an active research agenda that leads to refereed publications. Seek external funding for research projects, individually or collaboratively, with faculty or local/state agencies. Mentor and advise students. Participate in departmental, college, and university service activities. Engage with the community and contribute to public scholarship. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD or other terminal degree related to a social science field such as criminal justice, sociology, or criminology must be completed prior to August 2, 2027. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching in multiple modalities, especially delivering online courses. Demonstrated potential for publishing in peer-reviewed journals. Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues and students from diverse backgrounds. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1) A cover letter 2) Current CV which clearly outlines practical experience in homeland security 3) A statement of teaching philosophy For full consideration, completed applications should be submitted by November 2, 2026. For additional information, please contact david.eichhorn@wichita.edu. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) cd832300 Last Name (required) 4dc9ef74 Email (required) 7d94fd43 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ab27d02e Last Name (required) 3c5c5564 Email (required) 3194a6d5 Job Alert 55d41d62 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any t