    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-medical-biomedical-manufacturing-and-automation-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor – Medical/Biomedical Manufacturing and Automation",
      "description": "Assistant Professor – Medical/Biomedical Manufacturing and Automation - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor – Medical/Biomedical Manufacturing and Automation - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor – Medical/Biomedical Manufacturing and Automation College of Engineering | Faculty Assistant Professor – Medical/Biomedical Manufacturing and Automation 499422 On Site Faculty Department: Industrial, Systems, and Manufacturing Engineering Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range $95,000 to $110,000/yr, commensurate with qualifications Work Schedule: Dependent on teaching assignment and research program needs; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Industrial, Systems, and Manufacturing Engineering in the College of Engineering invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Medical/Biomedical Manufacturing and Automation. We seek an innovative scholar and educator who will contribute to our academic programs and research profile. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop a productive research program, and provide service to the university and profession. This position is a 9-month appointment with an anticipated start date of Fall 2027. Since 1928, Wichita State's College of Engineering has built a reputation for equipping engineering and computing students with the most complete education possible. From hands-on research using the latest technologies to our location in Kansas' center of industry — with virtually unlimited jobs, applied learning and professional connections — Shocker engineering students have everything they need to make their dream careers a reality. The Department of Industrial, Systems, and Manufacturing Engineering comprises 11 faculty, five degree programs (two bachelor’s, two master’s, and one PhD), and six graduate certificate programs. The department is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and student success. New faculty will find supportive colleagues and opportunities to engage in interdisciplinary initiatives across the university. The Biomedical Engineering (BME) program at Wichita State University is dedicated to preparing the next generation of engineers who will transform healthcare through innovation, research and collaboration. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and/or graduate level in advanced manufacturing. This includes designing curriculum and instructional materials, delivering high-quality instruction in various modalities (in-person, online, or hybrid), and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising research projects or theses/dissertation as appropriate, and incorporate applied learning opportunities (e.g. projects with industry or community partners) into the coursework whenever possible. Research/Scholarly Activity: Establish and maintain an active research program in medical/biomedical manufacturing (focused on advanced therapeutics and pharmaceutical manufacturing), advanced manufacturing, human-robot collaboration, automation, additive manufacturing and/or physical AI. This includes publishing peer-reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. The faculty member is expected to seek external funding (grants or industry collaboration) to support research activities and, where applicable, engage in interdisciplinary projects or partnerships with industry. Excellence in scholarship should be demonstrated by a record of research accomplishments or clear potential for high-quality research output. Service: Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession (e.g. reviewing for journals, involvement in academic societies). Other: Fulfill other duties as assigned, in accordance with the faculty member’s talents and departmental needs. All Wichita State faculty are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements An earned doctorate (Ph.D.) in Industrial Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, or a closely related field is required by August of 2027. Applicants who are at an advanced stage of their doctoral studies will be considered if they provide strong evidence that all degree requirements will be completed prior to June 2027. Teaching: Demonstrated potential for effective teaching in medical/biomedical manufacturing (focused on advance therapeutics and pharmaceutical manufacturing), advanced manufacturing, human-robot collaboration, automation, additive manufacturing and/or physical AI. Evidence may include prior teaching experience, student evaluations, teaching awards, or a teaching philosophy that reflects best practices in instruction. Research Ability: Demonstrated potential for effective research and scholarship. This can be shown by publications, conference presentations, independent work as PI/co-PI on funded projects, or other scholarly activities indicating the ability to develop an independent research program. All requirements should be verifiable. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent written and oral communication skills, and the ability to work effectively with colleagues and students. The candidate should be able to collaborate in a collegial academic environment and adapt to the interdisciplinary and applied learning focus of Wichita State. Evidence could include references and examples of written communication. Ability to build professional relationships within the community and across the university at all levels. Ability to provide instruction of curriculum to a variety of learners. Commitment to collaborative processes and environments. Preferred Qualifications: Interdisciplinary/Applied Focus: Experience or interest in interdisciplinary work or industry collaboration. For example, a history of working on research projects across disciplines or partnerships with industry and the community (aligned with Wichita State’s emphasis on applied learning and innovation) is desirable. Healthcare focus: Demonstrated evidence of experience in medical device manufacturing (focused on advance therapeutics and pharmaceutical manufacturing) that align with WSU’s National Institute for Health Solutions and Innovation (NIHSI). Additional Information: Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. Cover Letter: A letter of application addressing how the candidate’s qualifications and experience align with the position, including a summary of teaching philosophy and research interests. Teaching Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing teaching approach and experience (including course topics the candidate can teach, mentoring experience, and any evidence of teaching effectiveness). Research Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) outlining current research accomplishments and future research plans. Emphasize how these might involve students or connect to interdisciplinary and industry-related opportunities at WSU. Priority review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. The appointment for this position is August 2027. Contact details For any inquiries about the position, please contact Dr. Deepak Gupta, Department Chair at deepak.gupta@wichita.edu or (316) 978-7758 or Dr. Bayram Yildirim, Search Committee Chair and Professor at Bayram.Yildirim@wichita.edu or (316) 978- 3426. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) e6ccdbdb Last Name (required) 53801b05 Email (required) db093a28 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) d68517af Last Name (required) 9142a474 Email (required) 06aea78c Job Alert e21ffd2d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 22dfba6e Last Name (required) 013f821c Email (required) a4979f82 Send This Job To: 5bc641b5 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" – Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant – Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) f761e730 Last Name (required) 575e39b6 Email (required) 6d75c5c0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the