    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-educator-assistant-teaching-professor-of-physics-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor of Physics",
      "description": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor of Physics - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor of Physics - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor of Physics College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor of Physics 499451 On Site Faculty Department: Physics Division of Mathematics, Statistics and Physics Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $55,000 to a maximum of $60,000 Work Schedule: M-F hours depend on class schedule;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story ​The Physics division in the Fairmount College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (LAS) of Wichita State University (WSU) invites applications for a full-time 9-month non-tenure-track assistant educator/assistant teaching professor of physics starting on August 2, 2027. The successful candidate will employ a variety of strategies to foster student learning including encouraging active learning, promoting an inclusive classroom environment, maintaining proper course-related records, and promptly providing students with feedback as to their progress toward meeting the course objectives. Teaching responsibilities will primarily include face-to-face instruction during the day or evening. A full-time teaching load consists of 12 credit hours per term, which typically corresponds to 3 courses or lecture sections. The Physics division at Wichita State University (WSU) is an exciting, collaborative place to work where opportunities exist with department colleagues and other colleagues from across campus. The department offers B.A. & B.S. degrees in Physics and a growing graduate program, including both M.S. and Ph.D. degrees. Recognizing the value of hands-on training opportunities, the department also supports undergraduate research projects where students gain valuable experience. While non-tenure-track, this position offers a clear path to a long-term career through WSU’s established faculty promotion system, providing opportunities for rank advancement within the track. The department currently has nine tenured or tenure-track faculty, two teaching faculty, one postdoctoral research associate, 25 graduate students, and ~50 undergraduate physics majors. The faculty-led research focuses on two main themes: condensed matter physics and the physics of the universe, including high energy physics and astrophysics. Wichita State University (WSU) is a public research university in Wichita, Kansas, United States. It is one of the fastest-growing research universities in the country, with $411 million in research grants and contracts. Wichita State University is the major urban research and innovation university in Kansas with an enrollment of 17,548 students. The university offers more than 60 undergraduate degree programs in more than 200 areas of study in nine colleges. The university's graduate school offers more than 50 master's degrees in more than 100 areas, a specialist in education degree, and 13 doctoral degrees. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate level, including introductory algebra- and calculus-based physics classes. This responsibility includes designing curriculum and instructional materials, delivering high-quality instruction in various modalities (in-person, hybrid & online), and assessing student learning. While the focus is on teaching the large lecture-based introductory physics courses, opportunities may occur to teach upper division physics courses such as modern physics, thermal physics, E&M, etc. Service: A part of the workload is dedicated to service tasks to the Department, College, or University. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department. The faculty member may also engage in service to the academic community (such as reviewing paper manuscripts or grant proposals). Research/scholarly activities: Research activities are not required as part of the workload expectations for this position; however, continued scholarly activity and professional development, including pursuing research involving undergraduate students, are encouraged. Other: Fulfill other duties as assigned, in accordance with the faculty member's talents and departmental needs. All Wichita State faculty are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree and Equivalent Experience in the Field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Master's degree in Physics or closely related area for Assistant Educator or Doctorate degree in Physics or closely related area for Assistant Teaching Professor. Experience teaching physics at the college level Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to effectively teach undergraduate physics courses, including lecture and laboratory courses Ability to work effectively in a highly collaborative, engaging, and dynamic environment comprised of individuals with a range of backgrounds, skills, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: Doctorate degree in Physics or closely related area. At least two years of college-level physics teaching experience. Preferred License/Certifications/Training: No licensure required. Professional development or training in college teaching, instructional technology, laboratory safety, or evidence-based teaching practices is preferred. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1. Cover letter: A letter of application addressing how the candidate's qualifications and experience align with the position, including a summary of teaching philosophy and relevant scholarly interests. 2. Complete Curriculum vitae 3. Teaching statement: Statement of teaching philosophy (1-2 pages) describing their conceptualizations of teaching and learning, teaching and assessment methods, and how their teaching practices will engage students from a range of backgrounds and experiences. Timeline Review of applications will begin on 15-Nov-2026 and continue until the position is filled. For best consideration, please submit all materials by 1-Nov-2026. The start date for this appointment is August 2, 2027. For any inquiries about the position, please contact Dr. Foudil Latioui at foudil.latioui@wichita.edu WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: No additional physical requirements Apply Now First Name (required) 90d78b1d Last Name (required) f8e25c2e Email (required) be19a4f4 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) e077ea36 Last Name (required) 4c236eb5 Email (required) aa56ab16 Job Alert ba5cbbb9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 33ae9dd7 Last Name (required) d25dffd7 Email (required) 18baba82 Send This Job To: a1fbedb7 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" – Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant – Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) b94efbc0 Last Name (required) d53ced2d Email (required) 3b143141 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a 