    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-educator-assistant-clinical-professor-and-director-of-transition-to-teaching-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching",
      "description": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching College of Education | Faculty Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching 499442 On Site Faculty Department: School of Teaching and Learning Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $80,000 Work Schedule: 8am to 5pm, Monday – Friday, with some flexibility for evenings and weekends as needed. Course offerings include Saturdays. Work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The School of Teaching and Learning in the College of Education at Wichita State University invites applications for a 12-month full-time assistant clinical professor of education and director of the Transition to Teaching program. We seek an expert in areas related to, but not limited to, alternative teacher education, preparing individuals who are changing careers to become teachers, and middle and high school teacher education. We are looking for a collaborative colleague to lead our alternative certification program in the School of Teaching and Learning and join an engaged and collaborative faculty at Kansas’s only urban public research university. The academic appointment for this position will be effective June 7, 2027. As a faculty member in the School of Teaching and Learning, the successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate level classes in the fall, spring, and summer as part of our alternative teacher preparation program. The new faculty member will also work with various populations of students, colleagues, and community, engage in grant seeking activities, and provide service to the program, department, college, university, and profession. About the University and the School of Teaching and Learning Wichita State University is located in the heart of the Midwest in the largest city in Kansas. Our beautiful 330-acre campus recently experienced rapid expansion, with renovation projects and new housing and campus life initiatives. Our enrollment of roughly 17,000 ranges from traditional undergraduate and graduate students to professionals adding new skills or changing fields. We have online programs and thriving campus life/residential students. The School of Teaching and Learning at Wichita State provides high-quality teacher training in early childhood, elementary, and middle/secondary fields. Over 90% of our students receive teaching contracts upon graduation and we are the major source of teachers in the Wichita metropolitan area. Within T2T, students complete their applied learning experiences in the classroom while maintaining employment as teachers of record while throughout their time in the program. Our faculty publish at the regional, national, and international level, present at major conferences in our respective fields, and serve on accreditation boards and professional committees. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties This position will lead the Transition to Teaching program in the School of Teaching and Learning. Faculty members share responsibility for programmatic and instructional decisions within and across program options. The position is a 12-month appointment and carries a 4:4 load for fall/spring semesters, with an additional 6 credit hours of teaching in the summer semester. The director receives a 1-credit release each semester as part of administrative duties for leading the program. The Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor position include 80% teaching of undergraduate and graduate level courses as assigned, with a focus on content specific pedagogy, research, capstone, and internship or field experience courses. This also includes mentoring and supervising T2T teachers in both years of the program and coordinating school placements. The faculty member will provide service to departmental, college, university, professional and community constituting 20% of this role. Primarily the service role will include the Director of the Transition to Teaching program: developing and maintaining relationships with local school districts and agencies; attend relevant meetings, maintaining student data, leading the program annual report, contributing to accreditation and university reports, and directing recruitment and retention for T2T program. The faculty member may collaborate with colleagues to seek grants related to alternative certification programs. This position requires regular on-campus presence at Wichita State University. The selected candidate must reside in Kansas within a reasonable commuting distance of the WSU main campus. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree or Equivalent Experience in the Field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements A Masters or Ed.D or Ph.D. in Education, in teacher preparation or related field, completed prior to start date. Experience in K-12 teaching Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Evidence of potential for excellence in teaching. Willingness to employ various strategies in instructional delivery and learning activities, flexible teaching methods, and applied learning approaches. Evidence of communication and interpersonal skills to work effectively with diverse students and colleagues. Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and professionals. Ability to work supportively with returning adult college students/career professionals. Ability to develop relationships with community partners to enhance supervision and coordination of school placements. Preferred Qualifications: Earned Ed.D or Ph.D. in Teacher Preparation-Secondary Education or related field. Three years’ professional-level 6-12 teaching experience. Previous university level teaching experience, including online teaching Evidence of working with adult college students. Experience mentoring pre-service or in-service teachers. Experience in university level course development and implementation. Evidence of leadership in education. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1. Cover letter including teaching statement 2. Curriculum Vitae Review of applications will begin on November 2, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) 11316cc5 Last Name (required) 4cbcabf2 Email (required) 35954e1e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! Fir