    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-biomedical-sciences-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences 499491 On Site Faculty Department: Department of Biological Sciences Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $70,000 Work Schedule: M-F 8-5; Variable dependent on schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Position Overview: The Department of Biological Sciences in the Fairmount College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Wichita State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Biomedical Sciences. We seek applicants with teaching and research expertise in the fields of Microbiology, Virology, Genetics, and/or Parasitology. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop a productive research program, and provide service to the university and profession. This position is a 9-month appointment with an anticipated start date of August 2, 2027. Department Description: The Department of Biological Sciences offers majors in Biology with either an Ecological/Environmental/Organismal or a Biomedical emphasis. There are approximately 340 undergraduate majors and the department’s Master of Science in Biology program currently includes 19 graduate students. There are 11 faculty members and seven full-time departmental support staff/administrators. The department is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and student success. The department is an affiliate of the Kansas Idea Network of Biomedical Research Excellence (K-INBRE). It houses modern laboratory space that includes analytical/molecular and cell culture equipment, microscopy and protein chemistry core facilities, an accredited animal facility, and access to the Kansas State University and Wichita State University High Performance Computing clusters. Core Responsibilities Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate level in the candidate’s area of expertise. This includes designing curriculum, delivering high-quality instruction, and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising undergraduate and M.S. research projects. Research/Scholarly Activity: Establish and maintain an active, externally funded research program in Microbiology, Virology, Genetics, and/or Parasitology involving undergraduate students and M.S. graduate students. This includes publishing peer reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. Service: Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession. Other: Fulfill other duties as assigned, in accordance with the faculty member’s talents and departmental needs. All Wichita State faculty are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate level in the candidate’s area of expertise. This includes designing curriculum, delivering high-quality instruction, and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising undergraduate and M.S. research projects. Research/Scholarly Activity: Establish and maintain an active, externally funded research program in Microbiology, Virology, Genetics, and/or Parasitology involving undergraduate students and M.S. graduate students. This includes publishing peer reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. Service: Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD in Biology or related field and must be completed prior to August 2027. Teaching experience is broadly defined i.e. teaching assistantships, mentoring, participation in course lectures, etc. Please clarify in your teaching statement. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to teach undergraduate and graduate classes in area of expertise. Effective written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Demonstrated potential to establish an independent and productive research program. Demonstrated ability or potential to work effectively in collaborative environments and engage constructively with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: Postdoctoral research experience is preferred, but strong candidates lacking postdoctoral experience will be considered. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1) Letter of application 2) Current curriculum vita 3) Statement of teaching philosophy and goals 4) Statement of research interests and goals 5) Copies of unofficial academic transcripts Applicants must apply by October 19, 2026 for full consideration. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) 10731fc7 Last Name (required) e3da2ab0 Email (required) 30be7272 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ff4cf924 Last Name (required) f4cc8cbe Email (required) e3b07dde Job Alert 9fb71c00 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) ac6620eb Last Name (required) a247e08a Email (required) 2429d55f Send This Job To: 7d3e920b Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" – Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? I