    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-cad-cam-hamr-operations-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant 499744 Student Department NIAR CAD/CAM Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 18 per hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Flexible with class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story NIAR’s Hub for Advanced Manufacturing and Research (HAMR) is seeking a student with strong communication, organization, and customer service skills to support facility operations. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties This role focuses on ensuring a smooth day-to-day experience for building occupants and visitors by checking and stocking amenities (e.g., coffee and soda supplies), assisting with events and tour scheduling and preparation, and supporting package/mail tracking and occupant notifications. Depending on building needs, the student may assist other staff, help coordinate activities for visitors and partners, and provide support throughout the HAMR facility. The position may also assist with general coordination tasks across HAMR and provide support for special events as needed. This position is ideal for students interested in gaining hands-on operations and customer service experience in a dynamic research environment. Under supervision, students will: • Support daily facility operations, including opening/closing procedures, cleanliness checks, and readiness of common areas. • Check, stock, and track amenities (coffee, soda, snacks, paper goods), monitor inventory levels, and coordinate reorders with staff. • Assist with scheduling and preparing for events and tours, including room reservations, A/V checks, signage, seating layouts, and setup/teardown. • Assist visitors and tour groups, manage check-ins, and provide wayfinding support. • Track incoming packages/mail and promptly notify building occupants; maintain logs and coordinate internal deliveries as directed. • Maintain shared calendars and documentation, including event schedules, inventory records, and standard operating procedures. • Support special events at HAMR with onsite logistics and customer service. • Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements • Strong communication and customer service skills. • Excellent organization, attention to detail, and reliability. • Experience with event setup or facilities support (preferred but not required). • Comfort with inventory management and basic tracking tools (e.g., Excel, SharePoint). • Basic knowledge of A/V equipment setup. • Ability to work collaboratively, take initiative, and meet deadlines. Additional Information Ability to lift and carry up to 25 lbs. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Students must have their own transportation, as some local travel between facilities may be required. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) b56be934 Last Name (required) f6b1e7e3 Email (required) f57ffd99 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9f5b3bcb Last Name (required) 97f0a77c Email (required) 4b6f8c34 Job Alert 564976fe Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 9765d43f Last Name (required) 4145e70f Email (required) 715632ce Send This Job To: c1a8dbfd Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" – Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, 