    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/manager-student-legal-services-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Manager, Student Legal Services",
      "description": "Manager, Student Legal Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States Manager, Student Legal Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Manager, Student Legal Services Student Affairs (College) | Staff Manager, Student Legal Services 499559 Staff Department: Student Legal Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range beginning at $108,200/yr, adjusted based on qualifications Work Schedule: Mon-Fri, 8am-5pm. Some weekends and evenings will be required to support events.;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Are you a legal professional seeking a meaningful leadership role that supports a healthy work-life balance? Would you be interested in a position that allows you to have a direct impact on student success? If so, Wichita State University is seeking a dynamic and experienced legal professional to serve as the inaugural Manager of Student Legal Services! This leadership role provides direct legal services to students and support of the strategic oversight of the newly established program. This position is ideal for a licensed attorney with courtroom experience, a strong public service orientation, and the ability to lead a small team in a dynamic, student-centered environment. The successful candidate will have strong communication, leadership, and program development skills. Job Summary Manage, coordinate, and administer the day-to-day activities of student legal services programs and services. Oversee the implementation and evaluation of student legal services, ensuring alignment with University goals and initiatives and compliance with applicable rules and regulations. Essential Functions • Provide legal consultations, advocacy, and full legal representation to eligible students on a variety of criminal and civil matters; including performing conflict of interest checks related to representation. • Design and conduct student education, training and outreach initiatives in alignment with programming goals and objectives. • Establish sustainable processes, key performance metrics, management tools and reporting capabilities. Utilize data to develop new or revise current programs and services. Communicate quality and progress metrics to department, staff, and/or stakeholders. • Cultivate new and expand existing strategic partnerships and lead initiatives to support program success. Consult with stakeholders to assess needs and ensure effective support. • Oversee program budget according to needs. Monitor and adjust plans as resource requirements change. • Supervise assigned staff; including performance management, work allocation, training, promotion and enforcement of internal procedures and controls, and problem resolution. Evaluate performance and make recommendations for staff actions. Required Education and Experience: Juris Doctorate degree from an American Bar Association (ABA) accredited institution and admission to the Kansas State Bar Four (4) years of experience as a practicing attorney, with one (1) year in a leadership role. Required License/Certifications/Training: Licensed to practice law in the state of Kansas. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Public speaking Legal writing and research Strong Interpersonal skills Document management Presentation Skills Regulatory compliance Report writing Risk Management Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Frequent 60-90% Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Frequent 60-90% Ability to interpret effectively, accurately and impartially, both receptively and expressively. Frequent 60-90% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Sedentary: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Sedentary work involves remaining stationary most of the time. Apply Now First Name (required) 514f3d89 Last Name (required) 73c4ef25 Email (required) d6608439 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) de3312e0 Last Name (required) dc967186 Email (required) 3c0415f1 Job Alert 54c4a45b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Student Affairs (College) Student Affairs (College) Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) baa651ca Last Name (required) 94fc8c86 Email (required) 5033efc1 Send This Job To: a5761082 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at an