    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-automation-research-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states-5e2b134b-de45-4ffb-8d97-786557cf16ce": {
      "title": "NIAR Automation Research Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR Automation Research Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Automation Research Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Automation Research Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR Automation Research Student Assistant 499576 Student Department NIAR ARC Robotics & Automation Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \"U.S. Person”. Job Story The NIAR ARC team is looking for a student assistant. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties As a member of our Robotics and Automation group, you will be responsible for developing and designing automated systems for industrial applications. Our team conducts research and design for a diverse range of clients and is dedicated to advancing the field of intelligent manufacturing processes. Examples include systems developed to perform, automated inspection, robotic processing, automated damage repair. Alongside developing these systems, you will be responsible for enabling digital twin technologies through simulation, verification, and closed loop sustainment. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements Pursuing a Bachelor' s or Master's degree. Enthusiastic and willing to learn from a variety of specialist in the field of intelligent manufacturing. Must be able to work a minimum of 20 hours a week. Ability to work well in a team environment and effectively communicate ideas and solutions. Self-motivated and able to work without constant supervision. Ability to lift and carry up to 25lbs. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) f6e19ba8 Last Name (required) 67730c6c Email (required) 9bd9f785 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 1fc08334 Last Name (required) 07e47f73 Email (required) 1a6e6d76 Job Alert f89d3c15 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 7c8bfda7 Last Name (required) 0a4bbabd Email (required) e6d7a85a Send This Job To: a88c495b Share Now! Ple