    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/applied-learning-student-assistant-advanced-computing-technologies-and-data-systems-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Applied Learning Student Assistant - Advanced Computing, Technologies, and Data Systems",
      "description": "Applied Learning Student Assistant - Advanced Computing, Technologies, and Data Systems - Wichita, Kansas, United States Applied Learning Student Assistant - Advanced Computing, Technologies, and Data Systems - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Applied Learning Student Assistant - Advanced Computing, Technologies, and Data Systems Research Administration | Student Applied Learning Student Assistant - Advanced Computing, Technologies, and Data Systems 499663 Student Department Information Technology Services Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay 15.00 per hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Between the hours of 8am -5 pm Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story Looking to gain hands-on experience with advanced computing, research technologies, and data systems while building skills that are highly valued in today's technology workforce? We are seeking Shockers who are interested in developing technical, analytical, and professional skills through a paid applied learning student position. This opportunity provides real-world experience supporting Wichita State University's advanced computing and research infrastructure, including high-performance computing (HPC) and research cyberinfrastructure services used by students, faculty, and researchers across a variety of disciplines. Students will gain experience working in Linux-based environments, assisting users, solving technical challenges, creating documentation, and supporting research-focused technology services. Through this applied learning experience, students will strengthen their problem-solving abilities, technical communication skills, and understanding of professional IT support practices while contributing to the university's research and innovation mission. Supervision and mentorship will ensure meaningful experiences that align with academic preparation and career goals. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Applied Learning position provides practice in developing technical and professional competencies through: • supporting users of research computing and data systems • troubleshooting account access, software environment, and system usage issues • applying analytical and problem-solving skills to diagnose and resolve technical concerns • working in Linux-based and scientific computing environments • creating, updating, and maintaining user documentation and knowledge resources • developing technical communication skills through interactions with students, faculty, and researchers • monitoring system status and escalating issues through established support procedures • gaining experience with research software ecosystems and computing workflows • maintaining accurate records of support requests, activities, and resolutions • collaborating with professional staff on projects that support research and instructional computing services Assistance may include responding to service requests, onboarding new users, developing training materials, documenting procedures, participating in technology-related projects, supporting workshops or outreach activities, and performing other duties as assigned. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements US Citizen Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 8cefff06 Last Name (required) 18b7d531 Email (required) e9b961b0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b336c67e Last Name (required) 92e9099c Email (required) f1c46e56 Job Alert e9f7b121 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Research Administration Research Administration Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 07364e6a Last Name (required) 2de40b84 Email (required) 37fe7f04 Send This Job To: d73b6cc1 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STO