    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-darc-electrical-design-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR DARC Electrical Design Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR DARC Electrical Design Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR DARC Electrical Design Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR DARC Electrical Design Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR DARC Electrical Design Student Assistant 497770 Student Department Engineering Design and Mod Team Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $14 - 22 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The Engineering Design and Mod Team is seeking a student assistant to assist with electrical design. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area in which the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties This position will support various diverse program efforts as an electrical design student assistant. Tasks include detailed 2d schematics of electrical systems, 3d routing and modeling of electrical systems, drawing creation, software tool automation, and modeling parts from existing diagrams, scans, and drawings. This role will utilize design handbooks, recommended practices, and industry standards to define engineering for electrical systems. The electrical design intern will primarily utilize Autocad, Siemens Capital, CATIA V5, and 3DX CAD software. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications Working towards a degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or Computer Science. Sophomore or higher preferred. Experience and interest in electrical systems, circuit analysis, and software automation. Experience with MATLAB, AutoCAD, Visual Basic, and Python programming. Prefer interest in CAD. CATIA V5, 3DX, or Solidworks. Experience with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Excellent writing and communication skills. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment, including but not limited to phones, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 9c77d50d Last Name (required) e21bb867 Email (required) ed74c9f6 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) ba50a4b3 Last Name (required) 07221bea Email (required) 52b935ba Send This Job To: 326144ad Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" – Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operat