    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/performance-facilities-applied-learning-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Performance Facilities Applied Learning Assistant",
      "description": "Performance Facilities Applied Learning Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Performance Facilities Applied Learning Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Performance Facilities Applied Learning Assistant College of Fine Arts | Student Performance Facilities Applied Learning Assistant 499014 Student Department Performance Facilities Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $14 Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Dependent on class schedule and availability Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Performance Facilities, part of the College of Fine Arts, manages performance venues including Miller Concert Hall, Wiedemann Hall, DFAC Outdoor Amphitheatre, Wilner Auditorium, and Welsbacher Theatre. These spaces support music and performing arts events, as well as campus and community group performances. The department also provides technical support (audio, lighting, staging) for events at venues like Lowe Auditorium, CAC Theater, Koch Arena, and WSU Commencement. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties This listing outlines general student employee roles and does not cover all possible responsibilities. Employees often work across multiple areas for varied experience. Some roles, like Video Streaming, and Audio Recording, may require relevant experience, though it's not mandatory. Related experience is helpful, and on-the-job training is provided for all positions. * Stage Operations - Assist with setup and management of stage needs for events as a Deckhand or Deck Manager, ensuring smooth and organized performances. * Front of House - Provide audience support as a House Manager or Usher, coordinating with event staff to ensure a welcoming experience for attendees. * Technical Operations - Offer sound, lighting, and video support for performances at fine arts venues and select campus locations. * Video & Audio Streaming/Recording - Assist with recording and streaming events as a Video or Audio Producer, Engineer, or Operator. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements No additional requirements Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Additional Information Student positions have flexible, variable hours based on availability, event needs, and staffing. No fixed schedules are offered, and maximum hours follow WSU policy. Immediate hire is possible, but applicants must already have a U.S. Social Security number and card. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) f87e8a5d Last Name (required) 78548599 Email (required) 7c63b0ed Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 90510a90 Last Name (required) 9e31e66d Email (required) f975cc78 Job Alert b3d0792d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) College of Fine Arts College of Fine Arts Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 5c646866 Last Name (required) 287bb90c Email (required) 3d8e72e7 Send This Job To: 23a72c87 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 543ed107 Last Name (required) fc640d9b Email (required) ce200d3e Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
