    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/senior-contracts-and-grants-specialist-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist",
      "description": "Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist Office of Research (College) | Staff Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist 499112 Staff Department: Office of Research Campus Location: Remote - Candidate must reside outside of the immediate Wichita metro area to be eligible for remote work. Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Position range begins at $61,169/year and is commensurate with experience. Work Schedule: Typically, 8:00AM – 5:00PM, Monday – Friday. Overtime as needed to meet deadlines. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story In this senior-level role, you will provide comprehensive pre-award support for primarily grant and contract applications submitted on behalf of Wichita State University. Are you a problem solver? Enjoy the challenge of multiple projects and meeting their deadlines? This position will be responsible for the development, implementation and oversight of pre-award grant and contract functions, including ensuring all applications comply with sponsor and University guidelines, and State and Federal rules and regulations. In this role, you will be part of a team that makes it possible for Wichita State and our industry partners to conduct research and projects that will improve and change the community of Wichita, health, education, and technology for Kansas, the US and possibly the world! Job Summary Writes, reviews, and negotiates complex contracts pertaining to grants, sponsored research, service activities and other initiatives. Facilitates complex grant proposal development and fund sourcing as well as campus training efforts. Researches and interprets regulations, guidelines, and standards and oversees the processing of complex contracts and/or grants. Essential Functions Writes, reviews, and negotiates complex contracts, grants, and other sponsored awards. Reviews, assembles, and submits complex proposals on behalf of the University. Delivers education and guidance to faculty, research staff, departments, and administrators in development of competitive proposals and award administration of projects as well as funding policies, rules, and regulations. Researches and facilitates compliance with University, state, and federal laws, policies, and regulations in the daily operations of the contract and/or grant lifecycle. Advises leadership regarding potential conflicts of interest and time and dispute resolutions. Assists with the production of reports, proposals, and analyses for the University and for federal, state, educational, and other funding and regulatory agencies. Collects and prepares required documentation for proposals and contracts. Develops and reviews budget pertaining to the sponsored awards. Required Education and Experience: Sixty (60) hours of college coursework in business administration Four (4) years of experience in supporting complex proposal submissions, or negotiating complex contracts and/or awards at a university, government, or complex organization. An additional 60 hours of college coursework can be substituted for two (2) years of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: Certified Research Administrator (CRA) or Certified Pre-Award Research Administrator (CPRA) Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: *Proficiency in negotiation and contract negotiation techniques sufficient to deal with high-level business, industry, scientific and/or government officials or proficiency in proposal and budget development experience. *Computer proficiencies to include word processing, spreadsheet, database, internet, and other forms of electronic communication. *Ability to multi-task, work cooperatively as part of a team and maintain high output when working autonomously. *Ability to provide excellent customer service. *Ability to multi-task with a common-sense approach to prioritizing. *Advanced grammar and writing, excellent verbal, interpersonal, analytical and communication skills. Additional Information: Remote work opportunities may be available. Candidate must reside outside of the immediate Wichita area to be eligible for remote work. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) d1ebb707 Last Name (required) d89de5c4 Email (required) b6036da0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ba8f2b3f Last Name (required) 0bcb8821 Email (required) 4cdf9303 Job Alert f620f4f3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Office of Research (College) Office of Research (College) Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 382e5cda Last Name (required) e0dea0bc Email (required) 74e66ef7 Send This Job To: 4105c159 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) f5d7dabf Last Name (required) fe9d95b1 Email (required) 4fed9102 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-instrumentation-technician-full-scale-structural-test-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR Instrumentation Technician - Full Scale Structural Test",
      "description": "NIAR Instrumentation Technician - Full Scale Structural Test - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Instrumentation Technician - Full Scale Structural Test - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Instrumentation Technician - Full Scale Structural Test NIAR Institute | Aviation, Staff NIAR Instrumentation Technician - Full Scale Structural Test 499142 Aviation Staff Department: NIAR Full Scale Structural Test Campus Location: Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: Typically Monday - Friday; 8:00 am - 5:00 pm. ; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \"U.S. Citizen”. Job Details NIAR’s Full Scale Structural Test team is seeking a skilled technician to support hands-on installation, calibration, maintenance, and repair of laboratory and test equipment. This onsite role plays a key part in ensuring safe, accurate, and reliable testing operations while assisting with troubleshooting, analytical measurements, procedural documentation, and student supervision. Job Summary Conducts and assists with installation, troubleshooting, calibrating, maintaining, operating, and repairing equipment Essential Functions Installs, troubleshoots, repairs, calibrates/adjusts, and maintains equipment. Performs preventative maintenance and/or analytical testing on equipment. Performs and/or observes measurement equipment tests. Supervises undergraduate and graduate students to ensure satisfactory completion of research projects Maintains, calculates and prepares reports and records. Establishes, updates, and reviews laboratory procedures according to appropriate standards and/or requirements. Provides training to staff as needed to ensure proper process implementation. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Two (2) years of related experience Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Understanding of equipment calibration standards, preventative maintenance, and basic troubleshooting methods. Knowledge of laboratory safety protocols and procedures, including documentation requirements. Familiarity with measurement equipment and data collection principles. Skill in installing, maintaining, repairing, and calibrating laboratory or testing equipment. Strong problem‑solving skills to diagnose mechanical or instrumentation issues. Ability to perform accurate analytical testing and record keeping. Ability to work safely in confined, elevated, loud, or physically demanding environments.Ability to interpret and follow technical procedures, standards, and equipment manuals. Ability to manage multiple tasks, prioritize assignments, and meet deadlines. Ability to manipulate tools and test instruments requiring fine motor dexterity. Physical Requirements: Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to interpret effectively, accurately and impartially, both receptively and expressively. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Apply Now First Name (required) bdd365e3 Last Name (required) 0f6db850 Email (required) 1caafa5f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP