    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-consultant-senior-loads-engineer": {
      "title": "NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Loads Engineer -",
      "description": "NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Loads Engineer - NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Loads Engineer - social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Loads Engineer NIAR Institute | Aviation, Temporary NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Loads Engineer 499068 Aviation Temporary Department NIAR Design, Analysis, Requirements & Certification (DARC) Location Wichita, KS-WSU McConnell Job Summary: The National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) at Wichita State University is a nationally known aviation research center, providing a wide range of services including research, design, testing, certification and training. This role provides senior-level leadership for an external loads engineering group, functioning as an independent contractor responsible for guiding the team through the development of aircraft-level load cases and documentation required for program milestones. This position emphasizes technical direction, coordination of team activities, and mentoring of engineers at varying experience levels. Some travel may be required. Job Responsibilities: • Lead a team of engineers responsible for aircraft-level flight and ground loads development • Establish team priorities, define technical approaches, organize work assignments, and ensure alignment with program schedule • Proficient with static and dynamic external loads development • Coordinate with Mass Properties, Flight Sciences, Stress, F&DT disciplines • Prepare and deliver high-quality technical reports and customer-facing material • Mentor junior and mid-level engineers, fostering skill development and communication • Provide proactive communication and status updates to leadership and customers • Work independently with minimal oversight while ensuring team performance • Domestic travel up to 10% may be required. Qualifications/Minimum Requirements: • Bachelor’s degree in Engineering • Ten (10) years of experience in External Loads • Leadership experience - leading an engineering team and acting as a technical focal • Familiarity with civil and/or military requirements • Demonstrated ability to meet schedule expectations • Excellent writing and communication skills • Experience with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) • Professional and diplomatic demeanor • Strong accountability and integrity • Experience mentoring of interns and junior engineers Preferred Qualifications (Desired Skills/Experience): • Software Proficiency – Matlab, Nastran, Femap, Python, and similar tools All services are pursuant to a Professional Services Agreement, which must be executed prior to being assigned work Apply Now First Name (required) 5730030e Last Name (required) 5e84334a Email (required) acbc32a3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 762ba68b Last Name (required) 107dc93f Email (required) 913d625c Job Alert ee12e692 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Aviation Temporary Aviation Temporary Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) ff0b1412 Last Name (required) f4b5682d Email (required) ae35ec08 Send This Job To: d6af4b8f Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 70740591 Last Name (required) 208f3d5d Email (required) 3219dc2d Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
