    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-atlas-scram-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR ATLAS SCRAM Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR ATLAS SCRAM Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR ATLAS SCRAM Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR ATLAS SCRAM Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR ATLAS SCRAM Student Assistant 499023 Student Department NIAR ATLAS Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The NIAR ATLAS lab is looking for a SCRAM student assistant. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties -Operate robotic systems equipped with pellet extruder/milling/AFP/FFP/LMD head attachments. -Operate NC programs for manufacturing operations. -Perform routine maintenance and troubleshoot issues with mechanical/electrical/pneumatic systems. -Program for additive and subtractive manufacturing processes. -Clean and maintain the cell and the surrounding areas routinely. -Assist program managers with projects moving through SCRAM cell processing. -Organize and catalog tools, spare parts, and implements. -Ensure proper PPE use and follow basic safety procedures to minimize accidents and harm to others within the work cell. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements -Excellent problem-solving skills and a deep understanding of engineering principles. -Able to work for 20 hours during school semesters and 40 hours during summer semesters. -Familiarity with hand and power tools. -Ability to complete forklift and gantry crane training. -Excellent spatial reasoning skills and mechanical aptitude. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 15753f71 Last Name (required) 27cd3e2d Email (required) f6021da2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6aea8041 Last Name (required) 4af5a32f Email (required) f5b22618 Job Alert 15cc2515 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 00436b6f Last Name (required) 40cf9d44 Email (required) 2bd68393 Send This Job To: de9a371c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita 