    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-camo-coordinator-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR CAMO Coordinator",
      "description": "NIAR CAMO Coordinator - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR CAMO Coordinator - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CAMO Coordinator NIAR Institute | Temporary NIAR CAMO Coordinator 498923 Temporary Department NIAR Center for Aircraft Modification and Operations Location Wichita, KS-WSU McConnell Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \"U.S. Person”. Job Story In a hangar adjacent to McConnell AFB that once housed Boeing Air Force One modification facilities, the CAMO team at NIAR provides production design, initial and Supplemental Type Certification, instrumentation installation, modifications and field support/repair. We are looking for a Coordinator to join our fast-growing team! Job Summary The CAMO Coordinator assists Operations department in removing barriers to the progress of the assigned work scope. Assists operations with workforce guidance and first line communication. Serves as a liaison to support functions including but not isolated to Engineering, Methods, Material Logistics and Quality. Coordinates meetings for Special topics that require cross-functional inputs. Manages and monitors governance for assigned work scope. Job Duties Serves as a subject matter expert in a functional area; educates staff to ensure consistent and equitable application of policies and procedures. Supports the programs and services provided by the CAMO by performing varied or related processes which may include creating and maintaining databases and websites, monitoring, facilitating, and enforcing compliance with established criteria, guidelines and standards, etc. Problem solves and trouble shoots to resolve issues. Provides education and/or training to ensure the effectiveness of the program. Compiles data and reports; provides status updates and reports as needed Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Ability to follow instructions and work in a fast-paced environment. Basic mechanical aptitude or interest in aircraft Reliability and responsiveness Team-oriented mindset Strong work ethic and initiative Safety awareness Time management and multitasking Preferred Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Experience in a warehouse, maintenance, or aircraft environment Familiarity with hand tools and basic shop equipment Forklift certification, or ability and willingness to obtain certification Environmental Factors Active aircraft hangar environment with exposure to noise, moving equipment, and varying temperatures. Requires use of personal protective equipment (PPE) such as safety glasses, gloves, and hearing protection. Additional Information This position requires a valid driver’s license Must be at least 16 years old Physical Requirements Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information Ability to stand/walk for extended periods. Apply Now First Name (required) c2253249 Last Name (required) aecd2b44 Email (required) 7da4507b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 517541a4 Last Name (required) 423f3915 Email (required) 8d4c2f88 Job Alert 44e18980 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 8d3aa2d0 Last Name (required) 82d8f990 Email (required) 25d29e67 Send This Job To: e12847d4 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) c2600661 Last Name (required) 1f0970ad Email (required) c815e380 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
