    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/athletics-general-ticketing-development-staff-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Athletics General Ticketing/Development Staff",
      "description": "Athletics General Ticketing/Development Staff - Wichita, Kansas, United States Athletics General Ticketing/Development Staff - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Athletics General Ticketing/Development Staff Administrative and Support | Student Athletics General Ticketing/Development Staff 498732 Student Department Wichita State Intercollegiate Athletic Association Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $10/hour Work Schedule M-F, Flexibility to work evenings, weekends, & holidays. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Wichita State athletics is searching for professional, service-focused individuals for our ticketing/development team. We deliver memorable experiences that connect all to Shocker Nation through a shared sense of pride and passion. Ticketing/development staff is responsible for providing high-level customer service to WSU Athletics stakeholders while executing day-to-day functions of intercollegiate athletics revenue generation practices. Job Duties Make outbound phone calls and handle inbound phone calls, as necessary. Work external events to include all WSU ticketed home events and select hosted events at WSU. Handle conversations in person and over the phone with donors and season ticket holders during office hours. Projects as assigned by Revenue Generation Leadership Required Education Additional Requirements Ability to work nights and weekends. Ability to stay in one position for long periods of time. Be responsible and organized with time. Ability to handle cash and balance. Ability to handle difficult conversations and situations when necessary. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in a Sales and Customer Service Environment. Additional Information Hourly staff will carry out administrative and technical tasks as it relates to functions of athletics ticketing and development. This includes but is not limited to customer service conversations, interacting with and problem-solving for stakeholders at WSU Athletics events, and maintaining a first-class experience for all WSU patrons. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position and/or traverse campus buildings, including stairs. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 1dd8479e Last Name (required) eea25924 Email (required) e2b64554 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b5a0879f Last Name (required) 874ad2ca Email (required) 886d4c80 Job Alert ac2e6a56 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Administrative and Support Administrative and Support Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 9d7d09ed Last Name (required) 7e69014c Email (required) 03a85984 Send This Job To: 7b1cfd7b Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 7649e8b6 Last Name (required) 88ed69c3 Email (required) a6e47398 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of 