    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/wsu-temp-plant-ecology-crew-lead-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "WSU Temp - Plant Ecology Crew Lead",
      "description": "WSU Temp - Plant Ecology Crew Lead - Wichita, Kansas, United States WSU Temp - Plant Ecology Crew Lead - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode WSU Temp - Plant Ecology Crew Lead College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Temporary WSU Temp - Plant Ecology Crew Lead 498442 Temporary Department Biological Sciences Campus Location Other Kansas Location Hire Type Full Time Pay $16 per hour Work Schedule Work times may vary depending on weather, but can generally be expected 8 hours, 5 days per work. Start time can vary from 5:00-7:00 am and ending around 1:00-3:00 pm. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Wichita State University is seeking up to five highly motivated technicians to assist in data collection for a collaborative research project investigating the response of plants, birds, and soils to different cattle grazing practices on Conservation Reserve Program (CRP) grasslands in Kansas and Colorado. Although grazing animals such as bison historically played an important role in native prairie, grazing is currently excluded or highly limited in many CRP sites related to native prairie. Our study will quantify potential conservation risks and benefits of cattle grazing on CRP sites located in tallgrass (Kansas) and shortgrass (Colorado). Job Duties Technicians will collect plant data in three-person sampling crews (two technicians and one lead graduate student). Each crew will be responsible for sampling a subset of sites (36) in our areas of interest in Kansas and Colorado. Reaching sites will require driving a few hours each day over paved and low maintenance (dirt, gravel) roads in relatively remote, rural areas. Duties include but are not limited to: collecting vegetation structural data, plant species abundance, and plant biomass; data entry and quality control; and equipment preparation and maintenance. Candidates must be willing to hike long distances into field sites through tall or short grass prairie while carrying equipment to reach sampling locations. Working hours will be spent almost exclusively in the field and involve early mornings, long hours when necessary, and maintaining motivation during variable weather conditions. Technicians must be able to transport themselves to field housing and ready to begin training and orientation in mid-late May 2025. Required Education This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Additional Requirements Possess a valid driver’s license and willing to drive rental field vehicles on gravel and muddy roads. Must be available for the entirety of the field season ~mid/late May to August 8th, 2025. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifications Academic training in and/or enthusiasm for biology and/or ecology. Previous experience with plant identification preferred, but not required. Fit to perform and keep up field work while maintaining exceptional work ethic in a variety of conditions, including heat, humidity, rain, biting insects, and poison ivy. Eager to work in remote, rural settings for long periods of time. Good interpersonal skills and willingness to work and live with other technicians and interact positively with CRP landowners. Attention to detail and able to closely follow a detailed data collection protocol. Additional Information for Posting Technicians will gain experience with plant identification and data collection techniques, interact with private landowners, and large-scale ecological research. The field position will end by August 8th, 2025. Shared housing will be provided near field sites in rural Kansas (St. John) and Colorado (Las Animas or Lamar). Rental vehicles will be provided for fieldwork transportation. Apply Now First Name (required) ab8402d8 Last Name (required) 23891800 Email (required) 4fb8dcb3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 7f0230af Last Name (required) 93bc8edd Email (required) f7b66985 Job Alert 39f7ca46 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 2f04933f Last Name (required) 24d758c6 Email (required) 79cea743 Send This Job To: 336470f6 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR A