    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-consultant-senior-design-engineer-structures": {
      "title": "NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Design Engineer- Structures -",
      "description": "NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Design Engineer- Structures - NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Design Engineer- Structures - social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Design Engineer- Structures NIAR Institute | Aviation, Temporary NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Design Engineer- Structures 498555 Aviation Temporary Department NIAR Engineering Design and Modification Team Campus Location Wichita, KS-WSU McConnell Job Summary: Since its inception in 1985, National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) at Wichita State University has made a name for itself as the most capable university-based aviation research center in the United States by providing research, design, testing, certification and training to the aviation manufacturing industry, government agencies, educational entities and other clients that can benefit from our services. NIAR is looking for a talented Senior Systems Design Engineer- Structures to support diverse customer programs. Responsibilities include: Developing detail and modification design concepts through final design. Designs will meet contractual/producibility requirements for end item deliverables including structural modifications, mechanical components, and primary and secondary structural detail/installation design for development and production purposes. Tasks may also include airframe structural configuration layouts, final installations, preliminary sizing, joint layouts and detail part design utilizing metallic and composite materials within the CAD system. CAD models, drawings and other documents in support of the product, participating in trade studies, creating and maintaining ICDs (interface control documents), and coordination with customers. Technical excellence and adherence to schedule of assignment area. Design activity includes primary structure, flight test and development structure, special mission equipment, and prototype development. Ability to discuss designs and issues with customers, including metallic/composite part design, systems integration, materials, finishes, and processes. Candidate should be able to discuss designs and issues with customers, including metallic/composite part design, systems integration, materials, finishes, and processes. Qualifications/Minimum Requirements: Ability to work on-site 80% of the time This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Bachelor’s degree in mechanical, structural, aerospace or related discipline with 10 years of experience High proficiency with 3D CAD tools (3DExperience, CATIA V5, Siemens NX, Solidworks) Familiarity with NASA and/or FAA structural design standards Experience with airframe structure design, special mission modification design, and prototypes Experience developing and modifying 3D models & drawings as well as MBD designs Strong understanding of GD&T, design fundamentals, and ASME standards (Y14.5, Y14.31, Y14.37, Y14.41) Proficiency in GD&T tolerance application and experience with statistical stack-up analysis Experience with designing metallic and composite parts using the appropriate CAD workbenches Experience with Microsoft Office (e.g., Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Professional and diplomatic demeanor Strong sense of accountability and integrity Excellent writing and communication skills Domestic travel up to 10 % may be required Experience in technical leadership and mentoring of interns and junior engineers Self-motivated and driven to produce high quality designs on schedule Preferred Experience: Experience leading small teams and/or as technical specialist Experience creating structural/mechanical layouts and concept designs Aircraft support/MRB experience Experience with customer-facing role. All services will be provided as an independent contractor, pursuant to a Professional Services Agreement, which must be executed prior to being assigned any work. Apply Now First Name (required) f57723dc Last Name (required) 04176d6a Email (required) fec543bd Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) d7244171 Last Name (required) 5363fe6e Email (required) f911481a Job Alert c8460a93 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Aviation Temporary Aviation Temporary Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 58c40913 Last Name (required) 174cac10 Email (required) ba94694a Send This Job To: cbb512f2 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 21ff47f6 Last Name (required) a797ccd5 Email (required) 9f9c516d Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
