    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-consultant-senior-stress-engineer": {
      "title": "NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Stress Engineer -",
      "description": "NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Stress Engineer - NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Stress Engineer - social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Stress Engineer NIAR Institute | Aviation, Temporary NIAR CONSULTANT - Senior Stress Engineer 498550 Aviation Temporary Department NIAR Engineering Design and Modification Team Campus Location Wichita, KS-WSU McConnell Job Summary: Since its inception in 1985, National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) at Wichita State University has made a name for itself as the most capable university-based aviation research center in the United States, providing research, design, testing, certification and training to the aviation manufacturing industry, government agencies, educational entities and other clients that can benefit from our services. This position will be an independent contractor consulting as a Stress Engineer with NIAR to support various diverse customer programs. This person will complete tasks that may include preliminary sizing, development of load paths, detailed analysis, certification and documentation required to support program objectives. Experience in both metallic and composite analysis is desired. Some travel may be required. Responsibilities: Perform stress lead tasks as required to support program objectives. Perform detailed stress analyses and document as required to support program objectives. Analysis of details including primary structure, secondary structure, flight test, flight controls, mechanical systems, interiors, and major modifications. Participate in mentoring of junior analysts as they develop their engineering skillsets. Work under minimal direction. Domestic travel up to 10% may be required. Requirements: Ability to work on-site 80% of the time This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Bachelors degree in Engineering Ten (10) years of stress analysis experience Experience with classical handbook analysis methods and Finite Element Modeling (Patran and Femap preferred) Experience with metallic and composite analysis methods Familiarity with civil and/or military structural design standards Experience in 3D CAD tools (Catia v5 or 3DE preferred) Demonstrated ability to achieve desired results within a defined schedule Excellent writing and communication skills Experience with Microsoft Office (word, excel, PowerPoint) Professional and diplomatic demeanor Strong sense of accountability and integrity Experience in technical leadership and mentoring of interns and junior engineers Desired Skills/Experience: Experience leading small teams and/or as technical specialist Aircraft support/MRB experience Experience with customer-facing role Experience with detailed modeling software (Abaqus, HyperX) All services will be provided as an independent contractor, pursuant to a Professional Services Agreement, which must be executed prior to being assigned any work. Apply Now First Name (required) 10993bb5 Last Name (required) 59314a8b Email (required) 4bf1eafa Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 71621ed1 Last Name (required) c57684ac Email (required) 4723aa14 Job Alert 706f0953 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Aviation Temporary Aviation Temporary Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR In