    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/ndi-technician-level-i-niar-atlas-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NDI Technician Level I - NIAR ATLAS",
      "description": "NDI Technician Level I - NIAR ATLAS - Wichita, Kansas, United States NDI Technician Level I - NIAR ATLAS - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NDI Technician Level I - NIAR ATLAS NIAR Institute | Staff NDI Technician Level I - NIAR ATLAS 498253 Staff Department: NIAR ATLAS Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Details ATLAS – the Advanced Technologies Lab for Aerospace Systems – is a multi-disciplinary manufacturing environment and engineering education program to prepare engineers and educators for the Factory of the Future and to aid the current workforce in seamlessly adapting to advancements in the workplace. We are seeking an NDI Technician Level I to join our team. Job Summary Performs non-destructive inspection on aircraft components, test articles, and detail parts using pre-approved procedures to identify and notify Level II and/or Level III Technician of any problems in a timely manner. May direct and/or train undergraduate and graduate assistants in the performance of daily laboratory activities with the objective of achieving optimal quality control, process implementation and project performance. Follows laboratory procedures and techniques according to appropriate standards. Essential Functions Performs non-destructive inspection on aircraft components, test articles, and detail parts using pre-approved procedures to identify delamination, voids, porosity, cracks, corrosion, and/or mechanical damage. Sets up, calibrates, and operates equipment for inspection. Conducts tests with appropriate NDI technique(s). Interprets, evaluates, and documents inspection results under the direct supervision of NDI Technician Level II or III. Identifies and notifies Technician Level II and/or III of any problems in a timely manner. Obtains and analyzes information skillfully. Edits and presents numerical data effectively. Follows laboratory procedures and techniques according to appropriate standards. Other duties as assigned. Required Education and Experience NDT technical program meeting SNT-TC1A, and/or NAS-410 Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to perform research in a laboratory setting. Ability to operate engineering laboratory equipment. Physical Requirements Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to inspect and/or surveil materials, equipment, reports, and/or incidents and identify any errors, needs and/or determining factors. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Apply Now First Name (required) 9a4ff1d4 Last Name (required) e499aa45 Email (required) d2c84283 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ca2def7e Last Name (required) fd916773 Email (required) efafae03 Job Alert 93a338b4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create 