    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/integra-technologies-software-engineer-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Integra Technologies Software Engineer Student Assistant",
      "description": "Integra Technologies Software Engineer Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Integra Technologies Software Engineer Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Integra Technologies Software Engineer Student Assistant Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Student Integra Technologies Software Engineer Student Assistant 498164 Student Department Ennovar Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Ennovar is looking for a student assistant software engineer to work at Integra Technologies. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Provide enhancements and bug fixes for OMS and related database interfaces. Includes PL/SQL, Python, Perl, Java, and shell scripts. Support personal computers and related peripherals in a professional manner. Troubleshoot and support network infrastructure; perform upgrades and assist with monitoring for potential issues. Install upgrades and configure network printing, directory structures, rights, security, and software on file servers. Analyze user requirements, procedures, and problems to automate processes and improve existing computer systems. Provide IT support for all systems in production areas, including printers, networking, tablets, and Windows-based systems. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements Enrollment in a Computer Science or related degree program Student must have completed their Introduction to Programming course. Preferred Qualifications Prior hardware and software experience Knowledge/Skills 