    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/integra-failure-analyst-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Integra Failure Analyst Student Assistant",
      "description": "Integra Failure Analyst Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Integra Failure Analyst Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Integra Failure Analyst Student Assistant Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Student Integra Failure Analyst Student Assistant 497937 Student Department Ennovar Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 -18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Set up environmental hardware and verify production test results. Troubleshoot and resolve environmental setup and production issues. Collect, format, and analyze environmental testing data for engineering review. Document findings, perform calculations, and present results to engineering staff. Assist in hardware development, including assembly and soldering from schematics. Support environmental stress programs for electronic components. Collaborate with engineering, customer service, production, and shipping teams to facilitate tasks. Follow technical instructions, specifications, and procedures with accuracy. Apply analytical and mathematical skills to interpret test results and ensure component reliability. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications Currently pursuing a degree in Electrical Engineering or Electrical/Computer Engineering (sophomore or junior preferred). Strong attention to detail and ability to detect small defects (e.g., bent leads within 0.004-inch tolerance). Effective communication skills and ability to collaborate across multiple departments. Proficient in interpreting technical data, performing calculations, and applying mathematical principles. Ability to manage time, prioritize tasks, and follow detailed technical instructions. Basic soldering and hardware assembly skills (preferred). Comfortable lifting and handling equipment weighing 5 lbs or more. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) bae4979a Last Name (required) 78724687 Email (required) a65e61ea Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) e8163871 Last Name (required) 821a6cfa Email (required) 9756b297 Job Alert 8925c552 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or cli