    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/ennovar-general-application-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Ennovar General Application",
      "description": "Ennovar General Application - Wichita, Kansas, United States Ennovar General Application - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Ennovar General Application Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Student, Temporary Ennovar General Application 496632 Student Temporary Department Ennovar Hire Type Part Time Pay $14 - $18 per hour Job Story Ennovar at Wichita State University has designed an employment model that meets partner needs and enhances the learning process for student employees by integrating education and employment. Joining the Ennovar team offers the opportunity to work a flexible schedule in a corporate environment, collaborating with industry professionals and gaining experience and contacts that will help you achieve your post-graduation career goals. If you are interested in working with industry partners in the fields of Computer Science, Engineering, Data Analytics, Cyber Security and Technical Support Services, this might be the place for you! We offer the opportunity to: • Apply knowledge and skills gained in the classroom to the real-world • Experience the corporate environment • Earn recognition and potential career opportunities with Partner Employers • Make critical professional contacts • Test drive a prospective career • Gain practical training and experience that provides the tools to help them land a career post-graduation • Improve confidence • Build skills in fields that are looking to hire new talent. Ennovar’s corporate partnerships include, but are not limited to, the following: • Deloitte • NetApp • Boeing AeroSystems • Textron Aviation • USD 259 • Independent School • Intrust Bank • Koch Industries • Sedgwick County • Integra Technologies Please Note: Employment is contingent upon the continued partnership and contract with the client company for which you will be providing services. Changes to or termination of the client contract may impact the duration of this role. Applicants may be subject to additional screening requirements, including company background checks and pre-employment drug screens, as part of the hiring process. Employment with some of the corporate partnerships requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Certain positions require applicants to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \"U.S. Citizen”. International Students must obtain CPT to work in a position with corporate partnerships. Apply Now First Name (required) 82657fbd Last Name (required) 848a0942 Email (required) 8a9b5422 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 1624dc94 Last Name (required) 850e1114 Email (required) 20fcbbe5 Job Alert f45ed866 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Temporary Student Temporary Department(s) Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 5d744953 Last Name (required) 970940e2 Email (required) 8c574a5d Send This Job To: