    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/boeing-production-kitter-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Boeing Production Kitter Student Assistant",
      "description": "Boeing Production Kitter Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Boeing Production Kitter Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Boeing Production Kitter Student Assistant Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Student Boeing Production Kitter Student Assistant 495472 Student Department Ennovar Tech Services and Solutions Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $14 - $18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story This position with Ennovar will be working onsite for Boeing. The project is focused on designing and implementing standard fastener kits. Standardized kitting of these fasteners and washers promotes a lean manufacturing process, while also providing better visual work instructions to assist newer mechanics when building parts. This position will support the shop by filling kits with fasteners and washers for daily production demand. The position offers flexible work hours. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Read standard identification numbers. • Identify the location of fasteners to fill kits from cell centers. • Communicate with mechanics on issues they have with an incorrect fastener, or if the fastener is oriented incorrectly in the foam, also any issues with defective fasteners needing to be replaced in a timely manner. • Be familiar with the positions on the line, to ensure the corresponding kits are given to the correct position. • Keep track of requests for cell centers to be replenished with fasteners, washers, etc. • Effectively use technical reference materials. • Ensure the correct number of kits are filled up daily, ready for the mechanic to use when they start work – this could vary but should stay consistent with how many units per day each position builds. • Communicate effectively with the team or Manager(s) to make certain cell centers have enough fasteners to fill the kits and perform “hot-shot” procedures by communicating with the standards team if there are inadequate fasteners. • Ensures that implemented process enhancements meet improvement targets. • Ability to lift 10-20 pounds as needed and stand for extended periods of time. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications • Good time-management • Communication skills to receive and understand work tasks. • Ability to solve problems and work under stress. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phones, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 1a44592a Last Name (required) c1fd4912 Email (required) d60a3268 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) bbad3843 Last Name (required) cae3990e Email (required) 9cf94e95 Job Alert 84322d02 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit