      "title": "NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R",
      "description": "NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R Strategic Engagement & Planning | Student NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R 499395 Student Department Veteran Student Support Services Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15/hr Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Mon - Fri, 12-5 (Flexible with class schedule) Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Are you a student who enjoys helping others, staying organized, and being part of a supportive campus community? Veteran Student Support Services (VSSS) is looking for a dependable and motivated Student Assistant to join our team! As a Student Assistant, you’ll be more than just an extra set of hands—you’ll help create a welcoming environment where military-affiliated and veteran students can find the resources, encouragement, and support they need to succeed in college. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Welcome students who visit the VSSS office and help create a friendly, inclusive environment. Assist with check-in, scheduling, and general office tasks. Help students connect with campus resources and VSSS services. Support outreach efforts, including flyers, social media, email campaigns, and student engagement activities. Assist with VSSS events, workshops, tabling, and student activities. Help maintain program materials, supplies, and an organized student lounge. Assist staff with data entry, filing, copying, and other administrative duties. Help create a comfortable space where veteran and military-affiliated students feel that they belong. Provide peer-to-peer encouragement and help students navigate campus when appropriate. Take on special projects that support student success and the VSSS program. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements Friendly, welcoming, and comfortable interacting with students. Dependable, responsible, and able to work independently. Organized and detail-oriented. Comfortable using computers and common office technology. Able to communicate professionally in person, by phone, and through email. Respectful of student privacy and sensitive information. Interested in supporting veteran and military-affiliated students. Willing to learn and contribute as part of a team. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications Currently enrolled Wichita State University student in good academic standing. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Excellent customer service and interpersonal skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and professionalism. Dependable, organized, and detail-oriented. Comfortable using Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook, Teams). Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Experience with event planning, customer service, or office work is preferred but not required. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) f8aff92f Last Name (required) 3266a123 Email (required) 3a1904ba Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b1a50181 Last Name (required) c3909fdc Email (required) 7cc6402f Job Alert 4a60a2d3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) c7915a11 Last Name (required) 37f80525 Email (required) 538fd99a Send This Job To: d6d9692c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NIAR Administrative Specialist - Advanced Materials & Manufacturing Join the NIAR Advanced Materials & Manufacturing team and help keep one of the nation’s leading research environments running smoothly. We’re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast‑moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you’re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on‑site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit. ITS Network Student Assistant The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State’s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Clinic Office Coordinator, Dental Hygiene At the heart of our state-of-the-art, 24-operatory Delta Dental of Kansas Foundation Dental Hygiene Clinic, the Clinic Coordinator serves as the face of the clinic and a vital resource for students, faculty, patients, and program leadership. Working under the general supervision of the Department Chair, this role oversees the day-to-day operations of a busy patient care environment, managing appointment scheduling, facility and equipment coordination, financial accounts, clinic purchasing and inventory processes, and patient records management. Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 92fa006b Last Name (required) 88bbc883 Email (required) dc494dca Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
