    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/graduate-teaching-assistant-indirect-wichita-kansas-united-states-ee4531bd-9036-4fd1-92c7-021d9071e1a0": {
      "title": "Graduate Teaching Assistant - Indirect",
      "description": "Graduate Teaching Assistant - Indirect - Wichita, Kansas, United States Graduate Teaching Assistant - Indirect - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Graduate Teaching Assistant - Indirect College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Student Graduate Teaching Assistant - Indirect 499307 Student Department Modern & Classical Languages & Literatures Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $3,750 per semester Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Monday - Friday, times variable dependent on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story A Graduate Teaching Assistant (GTA) focused on indirect teaching supports academic courses behind the scenes without leading front-of-class lectures, centering on grading, course material preparation, and Blackboard administration. The primary function of a graduate teaching assistant (GTA) is to assist with instruction. GTAs have the latitude to make independent decisions, use judgment and exercise discretion when dealing with student matters. The main purpose and responsibility of GTAs is to impart knowledge or training to students at Wichita State University Job Summary The primary function of a graduate teaching assistant (GTA) is to assist with instruction. GTAs have the latitude to make independent decisions, use judgment and exercise discretion when dealing with student matters. The main purpose and responsibility of GTAs is to impart knowledge or training to students at Wichita State University. Required Education Bachelor's Degree Additional Requirements Grading & Assessment: Score quizzes, exams, essays, and homework assignments accurately using provided rubrics and answer keys. Course Material Setup: Help Faculty organize and format syllabus content, lecture slides, reading lists, and multimedia resources under faculty direction. Blackboard Administration: Help Faculty manage the online course portal (Blackboard), post announcements, update digital gradebooks, and upload files. Student Support Services: Help Faculty hold non-instructional office hours or virtual help desks to answer student questions regarding grades, logistics, or assignment formatting. Requirements & Qualifications Enrollment Status: Current active enrollment in a relevant graduate degree program (Master's) at Wichita State University. Academic Standing: Maintain a minimum cumulative GPA (typically 3.0 or higher) and good academic standing in the department. Required Experience To be eligible for an assistantship, students must be admitted to a degree program in either full or conditional standing. Students admitted on probation or placed on academic probation following admission may be eligible for assistantship awards under certain circumstances. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 1db001b1 Last Name (required) 855c81b4 Email (required) f8e2dc32 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b6523242 Last Name (required) b1e61306 Email (required) 290f8bf5 Job Alert 3cf6fa2a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) College of Liber