    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/academic-advisor-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Academic Advisor - Wichita, Kansas, United States Academic Advisor - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Academic Advisor Strategic Engagement & Planning | Academic/Student Support, Staff Academic Advisor 499848 Academic/Student Support Staff Department: TRIO STEM SSS Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Starting at $20.48 per hour, commensurate with experience Work Schedule: General business hours; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Advises students concerning their academic plans, progress, and academic and career goals in order to assist students in making personal education decisions and meeting graduation requirements. Interprets student needs and provides individualized service and assistance while maintaining confidentiality. Job Summary Advises students concerning their academic plans, progress, and academic and career goals in order to assist students in making personal education decisions and meeting graduation requirements. Interprets student needs and provides individualized service and assistance while maintaining confidentiality. Essential Functions • Provides students with information on how to complete their college degree and refers students to appropriate campus and community services and resources when needed. • Serves as a resource person to faculty and others with regard to academic advising policies and procedures. May review and optimize procedures as needed. • May assist in the development of and participates in recruitment and retention activities related to the student population such as monitoring educational progress and/or providing application or other assistance. May maintain confidential student records and personal information. • May conduct or participate in seminars, workshops or orientation sessions for students on academic, career and personal success strategies and other group activities. Job Duties Required Education and Experience: Qualifications for this position are strictly defined by the approved grant proposal. See the education qualifications in the \"Additional Information for Posting\" section below. Qualifications for this position are strictly defined by the approved grant proposal. See the experience qualifications in the \"Additional Information for Posting\" section below. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge advising individuals from disadvantaged diverse populations; Good presentation skills; Advanced computer skills including Microsoft applications and database experience; Excellent communication and analytical skills; Familiar with higher education &/or providing academic, graduate school, career, and financial literacy advising; Knowledge of federal and state regulations affecting persons with disabilities; Knowledge of basic counseling principles/strategies; Knowledge of issues concerning first-generation, low-income and college STEM students. Additional Information: Required Minimum Education: Bachelor’s degree in Student Personnel, Education, Administration, Counseling or a related discipline. Required Minimum Experience: at least one (1) year of experience advising individuals from disadvantaged diverse populations. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Frequent 60-90% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Frequent 60-90% Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) b70355b9 Last Name (required) 5198f995 Email (required) a05dca45 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b76acc26 Last Name (required) ae3f15d1 Email (required) b1b47d75 Job Alert 2cfa0dd5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic/Student Support Staff Academic/Student Support Staff Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs OMER GRA Position This position will work mainly with Dr. Sue Abdinnour in the FREDS department in the Barton School of Business. Marketing & Communications Graduate Assistant Are you passionate about marketing, social media, writing, design, and creating content that captures attention? Join the College of Education as a Marketing and Communications Graduate Assistant and gain real-world experience managing social media campaigns, producing photo and video content, designing promotional materials, writing news stories, email communications, and other marketing content, editing and designing website content, and helping grow the college's brand. This hands-on role is ideal for a creative graduate student with strong writing, content creation, graphic design, and digital communication skills who wants to build an impressive marketing portfolio while making a meaningful impact on student engagement and recruitment for the College of Education. College Access Mentor - Wichita Kansas Kids @ GEAR UP is a state-wide program serving students in foster care, grades 7-12 and first year in college. This is NOT a remote position - check the job location before applying! Executive Assistant to the President's Office The President's Office is seeking a discerning, astute & industrious person to handle the dynamics this position presents. Someone who can bring order to a fast-moving environment without slowing it down. We need exceptionally organized professional who understands that supporting university leadership takes more than managing a calendar. It takes anticipation, sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to see how all the moving pieces fit together. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 55f8b0dd Last Name (required) c7f4ab24 Email (required) 91703377 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on ou