    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-teaching-professor-main-campus-wichita-kansas-united-states-3db64ab4-b1c7-434f-a3ff-af74a148ac4b": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus College of Health Professions | Faculty Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus 499760 On Site Faculty Department: The Ascension Via Christi – Wichita State University School of Nursing Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Starts at $67,000 Work Schedule: Typically M-F 8-5, occasional weekend or evening shift; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Ascension Via Christi – Wichita State University School of Nursing is accepting applications for a 9-month Assistant Teaching Professor (DNP prepared) to provide instruction of didactic, clinical and/or technologies labs, and teaching/supervision in the undergraduate/graduate program as appropriate by educational preparation. This position will also participate in curriculum development and evaluation and will be expected to maintain academic and professional expertise. Participation in Department, College, and University activities and committees is expected. The nursing program is very robust with a traditional RN program, an RN-BSN completion program, and Masters’ program with a focus on education, and a DNP program with foci in FNP, PMHNP, and AGPNP. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree Teaching experience Faculty Requirements DNP (Doctor of Nursing Practice) Valid Kansas State APRN License Valid Kansas State Nursing License Nurse Practitioner Certificate Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent interpersonal skills Excellent verbal and written communication skills Computer competency Knowledge of clinical practice Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position – Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators – Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) 621303c1 Last Name (required) 01343eca Email (required) 0aa87948 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) cc8b4704 Last Name (required) 8dc246c7 Email (required) e8824f18 Job Alert 754e9117 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Health Professions College of Health Professions Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number