    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/marketing-communications-graduate-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Marketing & Communications Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Marketing & Communications Graduate Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Marketing & Communications Graduate Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Marketing & Communications Graduate Assistant College of Education | Student Marketing & Communications Graduate Assistant 499893 Student Department College of Education Dean's Office Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $3,840-$4,480 per semester Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Determined with supervisor, based on need and class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Are you passionate about marketing, social media, writing, design, and creating content that captures attention? Join the College of Education as a Marketing and Communications Graduate Assistant and gain real-world experience managing social media campaigns, producing photo and video content, designing promotional materials, writing news stories, email communications, and other marketing content, editing and designing website content, and helping grow the college's brand. This hands-on role is ideal for a creative graduate student with strong writing, content creation, graphic design, and digital communication skills who wants to build an impressive marketing portfolio while making a meaningful impact on student engagement and recruitment for the College of Education. Job Summary A Graduate Staff Assistant (GSA) assistants university service and academic units in either non-teaching or non-research activities. Specific duties of the GSA vary widely, depending on the administrative or academic unit to which they are assigned, but should be at a level to make use of their education and abilities. Job Duties The Marketing & Communications Graduate Student Assistant will play a vital role in supporting the College of Education's marketing and communication efforts. This position offers a valuable opportunity for hands-on experience in various aspects of communications and marketing. The successful candidate will work closely with the marketing and communications team to execute strategies that enhance the college's brand, engage its audience, and promote its programs and initiatives. Responsibilities: 1. Content Creation: Assist in developing engaging content for various communication channels, including social media, newsletters, website, promotional materials, and more. 2. Graphic Design: Create visually appealing on-brand materials to support marketing campaigns and communication materials. 3. Photography and Video Production: Assist in attending events or planned photoshoots to capture photos and video content. Basic photo and video editing. 4. Social Media Management: Contribute to the planning and execution of social media campaigns to increase brand awareness, engagement, and followership across platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, Twitter (X), and LinkedIn. 5. Website Editing: Complete University web training sessions, assist with website maintenance, design and editing. 6. Writing: Draft copy for news stories, feature articles, emails, social media posts, and other communication channels, adhering to brand voice and messaging guidelines. Assist in writing for internal and external news outlets (newsletter items, press releases). 7. Event Coordination/Support: Provide promotional support for college events, including virtual and in-person seminars, workshops, and information sessions. 8. Market Research: Conduct research to identify trends, competitors, and opportunities in the higher education landscape, informing marketing strategies and decision-making. 9. Analytics and Reporting: Assist in tracking and analyzing the performance of initiatives via social media analytics and email marketing platforms. Prepare regular reports with key insights and recommendations for optimization. 10. Administrative Support: Provide general administrative support to the Communications and Marketing team, including scheduling meetings, organizing files, and responding to inquiries. Required Education Bachelor's degree Additional Requirements 1. Currently enrolled in a graduate program in Communications, Marketing, Graphic Design, Public Relations or a related field. 2. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a keen attention to detail and grammar. 3. Proficiency in graphic design software such as Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign) and Canva. 4. Familiarity with social media platforms and trends, with experience in managing social media accounts for organizations. 5. Basic understanding of marketing principles and strategies. 6. Ability to work independently and collaboratively, managing multiple tasks and deadlines effectively. 7. Prior experience in communications, marketing, or related fields through internships, coursework, or extracurricular activities. 8. Analytical mindset with the ability to interpret data and draw actionable insights. 9. Commitment to upholding the college's values and mission, with a passion for higher education and student success. Required Experience To be eligible for an assistantship, students must be admitted to a degree program in either full or conditional standing. Students admitted on probation or placed on academic probation following admission may be eligible for assistantship awards under certain circumstances. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 033902ff Last Name (required) 5dccbf47 Email (required) 3c344846 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 58da016f Last Name (required) 5e1923e6 Email (required) 7486d180 Job Alert ef80c5e4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) College of Education College of Education Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) aa8e2a47 Last Name (required) 687084c6 Email (required) c509a5c8 Send This Job To: 57c32f06 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs OMER GRA Position This position will work mainly with Dr. Sue Abdinnour in the FREDS department in the Barton School of Business. College Access Mentor - Wichita Kansas Kids @ GEAR UP is a state-wide program serving students in foster care, grades 7-12 and first year in colleg