    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/executive-assistant-to-the-president-s-office-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant to the President's Office",
      "description": "Executive Assistant to the President's Office - Wichita, Kansas, United States Executive Assistant to the President's Office - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Executive Assistant to the President's Office President's Organizations | Office/Administrative Support, Staff Executive Assistant to the President's Office 499871 Office/Administrative Support Staff Department: President's Office Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range begins at $61,000/yr (negotiated based on qualifications) Work Schedule: General business hours with required attendance regular nights & weekends; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The President's Office is seeking a discerning, astute & industrious person to handle the dynamics this position presents. Someone who can bring order to a fast-moving environment without slowing it down. We need exceptionally organized professional who understands that supporting university leadership takes more than managing a calendar. It takes anticipation, sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to see how all the moving pieces fit together. The significant portion of the position focuses on coordinating the schedule & activities of the President and his household, and the broader needs of his office as well as the Provost. We need someone experienced with what it takes & stays up to date with basic evolving office technology. You will need to manage a constant flow of requests, conversations, & competing priorities from across the university to seamlessly coordinate into an ever-changing schedule. Your job is to track all the moving pieces of the office, stay organized, shift with competing or quickly changing deadlines all while ensuring the end result is as expected. You’re not just keeping the calendar; you’re thinking three steps ahead. Calm under pressure. Confident with people. Always one step ahead. When all the burners are going, nothing burns and nothing boils over. Your composure, organization, and foresight to manage the unexpected while ensuring the expected still gets done. Take your chance to join a hardworking office that keeps Wichita State growing, innovating & remaining as a top competitor for students across the nation! Job Summary Provides administrative professional support for the President and executive staff which may include, but is not limited to, scheduling and appointments; coordination of meeting and events; travel arrangements; preparing and editing correspondence, presentations, and reports, and preparing expense reimbursements. Essential Functions • Maintains President, Vice President(s), and executive staff schedules by planning and scheduling meetings, conferences, teleconferences. Prepares and edits correspondence, presentations and reports, and prepares expense reimbursements. May make related travel arrangements. • Coordinates events and schedules for the President's family. May coordinate professional meetings and events which may include, but is not limited to, catering, guest lists, entertainment, supplies, reservations, and set up. • Coordinates with state-contracted government relations personnel for President and executive staff. • Manages guest relations for sporting events hosted by the President and Governmental Relations. Manages the President's skybox at Eck Stadium and all events at the President's residence. Coordinates maintenance of home and grounds. • Presides as the Assistant Secretary to the Board of Trustees (BOT) with planning and coordination of meetings, transcribing of minutes, managing action items, maintaining records, communicating and corresponding with members of the BOT and President's Council. • Interacts with faculty, staff, alumni, government officials and high-level University, business, city, county and state administrators. • Exercises discretion, confidentiality, and judgment when dealing with matters of a sensitive, confidential or personal nature. • Supervises President's Office student assistants. Required Education and Experience: 60 hours of college coursework in business administration. Six (6) years of experience working for a high-level executive, executive office setting or related field. An additional 60 hours of college coursework can be substituted for two (2) years of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Advanced administrative knowledge and technical proficiency. Core transferrable skills and strategic capabilities to act as a reliable partner to senior leadership. Ability to anticipate needs of the office &/or the executive team. Proficient with executive scheduling as well as booking flights and hotels. Knowledgeable handling invoices & processing of those related to policies that govern. Exceptional communication skills congruent with executive members, state leaders & other high-priority stakeholders. Methodical organizational skills utilized constantly. Ability to be flexible & shift as needed for the office, President's or priority's needs. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in business or related field Four years of experience working for a high level executive, executive office setting or related field. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) d49f4a7a Last Name (required) a2a8a39c Email (required) a4365b96 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4304bb8f Last Name (required) c3558692 Email (required) 93def9d2 Job Alert 42c246ca Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Office/Administrative Support Staff Office/Administrative Support Staff Department(s) President's Organizations President's Organizations Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) c54f1529 Last Name (required) dce9c39c Email (required) a1f5512e Send This Job To: bc7023d5 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs OMER GRA Position This position will work mainly with Dr. Sue Abdinnour in the FREDS department in the Barton School of Business. Marketing & Communications Graduate Assistant Are you passionate about marketing, social media, writing, design, and creating content that captures attention? Join the College of Education as a Marketing and Communications Graduate Assistant and gain real-world experience managing social media campaigns, producing photo and video content, designing promotional materials, writing news stories, email communications, and other marketing content, editing and designing website content, and helping grow the college's brand. This hands-on role is ideal for a creative graduate student with strong writing, content creation, graphic design, and digital communication skills who wants to build an impressive marketing portfolio while making a meaningful impact on student engagement and recruitment for the College of Education. College Access Mentor - Wichita Kansas Kids @ GEAR UP is a state-wide program serving students in foster care, grades 7-12 and first year in college. This is NOT a remote position - check the job location before applying! Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" – Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) d98fb131 Last Name (required) e05a1b65 Email (required) fea96036 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you C