    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/pathfinders-housing-and-residence-life-wichita-kansas-united-states-a89abffd-c617-40ea-a5bd-638da3fdc3c3": {
      "title": "Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life",
      "description": "Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life - Wichita, Kansas, United States Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life Student Affairs (College) | Academic/Student Support, Student Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life 499877 Academic/Student Support Student Department Housing and Residence Life Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $10/hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Variable dependent upon class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The Pathfinders’ position is a vital member of the Residence Life staff. Pathfinders contribute to residents' education by serving as mentors, role models, and academic resources, and by connecting them with other key departments across campus. The Pathfinders will play a key role in fulfilling the academic mission of the Housing and Residence Life department. It is important that Pathfinders develop and maintain open lines of communication with faculty and staff involved in LLC and Housing and Residence Life. To achieve these goals, the Pathfinders must be actively engaged with students in their LLC and with various campus departments. This person will report directly to the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement or designee. In addition, the Pathfinders will work closely with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Community Development Responsibilities • Assist residents in formulating academic objectives concurrent with their individual interests and potential skill levels. • Provide residents with information regarding registration, drop/add, and curricular requirements. • Facilitate opportunities for residents to develop in the areas of learning styles, study skills, and test-taking. • Facilitate review sessions, study hours, and other academic support activities for students on the floor. • Establish and maintain appropriate relationships with students in the LLC for the purpose of facilitating the transition to university life and ensuring academic success. • Provide opportunities for developing skills in choosing an academic major and planning a career. • Act as a referral agent by directing students, when appropriate, to various academic support services such as Academic Advising, the Writing Center, the Math Lab, and the Student Success Center. Administrative Responsibilities • Participate in training workshops prior to the beginning of each semester and throughout the academic year. • Help run events during Week Zero. • Attend and participate in staff meetings and one-on-ones. • Facilitate LLC educational programming for residents monthly. • Create and maintain one bulletin board in the building, changing it monthly. • Provide assistance to, and communicate with, faculty, staff members, and LLC Coordinators. • Become knowledgeable about academic services available to students and make appropriate referrals. • Actively participate in LLC floor, university/college programs, and activities, and facilitate residents’ involvement with the same programs and activities. • Work closely with the LLC Coordinators to build community and accomplish academic initiatives. • Work closely with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement to accomplish residence life goals and to ensure that the interests of participating students are integrated into the program. • Serve as a liaison between residents in LLC and other departments, specifically within the Division of Campus Life, Academics, and LLC Coordinators. • Assume other responsibilities related to the LLC floor and residence life programs as directed by the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements • May carry a maximum academic course load of 16 hours during each semester of employment. Any exception must be approved in writing by the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement. • Be available for training the week before move-in. • Must maintain a minimum cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5 during the period of employment. • Attend and participate in one-on-ones with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement or designee. • Attend and participate in staff meetings. • May not engage in additional part-time or full-time work, student teaching, internship, or assistantship without prior written approval from the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications • Possess a motivating interest in working with the students in Shocker Hall. • Have a minimum cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5 on a 4.0 scale. • Be available to serve on the staff for two (2) consecutive semesters (Fall & Spring). • Have lived in a WSU residence hall for at least one (1) semester. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 1d704a12 Last Name (required) 56fc60bf Email (required) 5c7555a1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to availa