      "title": "Writing Specialist, TRIO SSS STEM",
      "description": "Writing Specialist, TRIO SSS STEM - Wichita, Kansas, United States Writing Specialist, TRIO SSS STEM - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Writing Specialist, TRIO SSS STEM Strategic Engagement & Planning | Student Writing Specialist, TRIO SSS STEM 499165 Student Department TRIO STEM Student Support Services Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $12.00 per hour, 10 hrs a week Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The writing specialist provides high‑quality academic support to undergraduate participants in the federally funded TRIO Student Support Services – STEM Program. Tutors assist students in strengthening their understanding of course content, developing effective learning strategies, and building confidence in their academic abilities. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Provide tutoring in writing for all disciplines, including essays, lab reports, research papers, and personal statements. Assist with brainstorming, outlining, drafting, revising, grammar, structure, clarity, and APA/MLA formatting. Support discipline‑specific writing needs for STEM students. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications Prior tutoring, teaching, mentoring, or peer‑education experience. Experience supporting first‑generation, low‑income, or students with disabilities. Experience with academic writing across disciplines. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) fc0ce4b6 Last Name (required) b82070be Email (required) b98d906a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 1c53a26d Last Name (required) 222c3487 Email (required) 821cb6ad Job Alert 5eb5430b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 1b72089b Last Name (required) 143f16dc Email (required) f3ad786b Send This Job To: 32dc800f Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message f