    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-statistician-wichita-kansas-united-states-fd4e16f4-91c9-451e-8987-09ac89457bb7": {
      "title": "NIAR Statistician",
      "description": "NIAR Statistician - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR Statistician - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR Statistician NIAR Institute | Aviation, Staff NIAR Statistician 499226 Aviation Staff Department: NIAR Composites and Structures Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Details The National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) is a fast-growing area within WSU, known globally for our expertise in the most critical areas of aerospace research and development. The Composites and Structures Lab is looking for a Statistician to join their team. If you are detail oriented, enjoy challenging and rewarding work, and like being part of a team, consider applying for this position! Job Summary Independently interprets, organizes, executes, and coordinates statistical research assignments in a field or specialization of an engineering discipline. Formulates and conducts research on problems of considerable scope and complexity involving statistically mature and unmature data sets. Explores subject area and defines scope and selection of problems for investigation through conceptually related studies or series of projects of lesser scope. Essential Functions Interprets, organizes, executes, and coordinates engineering research assignments concerned with unique or controversial statistical problems. Applies diversified knowledge of statistics research principles, practices, and protocols in research projects; makes recommendations and conclusions which serve as the basis for decision making in a specialty area. Formulates and conducts systematic problem analysis and resolution in an area of considerable scope and complexity through a series of complete and conceptually related studies, or through a variety of projects of lesser scope. Receives administrative supervision, with assignments given in terms of broad general objectives and limits for specific statistically related projects. Follows and manipulates statistical model concepts and approaches as an individual researcher and acts independently on technical matters. Collaborates with users and principal investigators on design, analysis, application, and reporting of statistical projects; provides technical leadership and technique consultation. Prepares analyses, reports, and assists with the preparation of, materials for grant proposals to obtain funding in support of research activities. Serves as investigator on single or multiple projects of complexity and scope consistent with above criteria, and/or manages a research unit. Maintains currency of knowledge with respect to relevant state-of-the-art technology, equipment, and/or systems. Required Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in engineering, math, or statistics related field Two (2) years of related experience in a statistician role Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to Interpret, organize, execute, and coordinate engineering research assignments concerned with unique or controversial statistical problems Ability to apply diversified knowledge of statistics research principles, practices, and protocols in research projects; make recommendations and conclusions which serve as the basis for decision making in a specialty area. Physical Requirements Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to position self to move and/or transfer materials, mail, equipment and/or supplies. Ability to move or traverse across campus, within buildings and offices, and/or across external environments. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to interpret effectively, accurately and impartially, both receptively and expressively. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Apply Now First Name (required) 3353a850 Last Name (required) 72d58a2e Email (required) 33ec88d7 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 0519a4ea Last Name (required) c041cfa6 Email (required) a5bf400c Job Alert 11a71a9d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Aviation Staff Aviation Staff Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 36b66d8d Last Name (required) 118ba250 Email (required) 0c32d9e6 Send This Job To: d768de55 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs OMER GRA Position This position will work mainly with Dr. Sue Abdinnour in the FREDS department in the Barton School of Business. Marketing & Communications Graduate Assistant Are you passionate about marketing, social media, writing, design, and creating content that captures attention? Join the College of Education as a Marketing and Communications Graduate Assistant and gain real-world experience managing social media campaigns, producing photo and video content, designing promotional materials, writing news stories, email communications, and other marketing content, editing and designing website content, and helping grow the college's brand. This hands-on role is ideal for a creative graduate student with strong writing, content creation, graphic design, and digital communication skills who wants to build an impressive marketing portfolio while making a meaningful impact on student engagement and recruitment for the College of Education. College Access Mentor - Wichita Kansas Kids @ GEAR UP is a state-wide program serving students in foster care, grades 7-12 and first year in college. This is NOT a remote position - check the job location before applying! Executive Assistant to the President's Office The President's Office is seeking a discerning, astute & industrious person to handle the dynamics this position presents. Someone who can bring order to a fast-moving environment without slowing it down. We need exceptionally organized professional who understands that supporting university leadership takes more than managing a calendar. It takes anticipation, sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to see how all the moving pieces fit together. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 7fba9ba2 Last Name (required) 339b4dce Email (required) 4a61914c Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
