    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/usd-259-tech-support-wichita-kansas-united-states-9f30d1fa-f197-4274-8cf1-03d8f7d63e8d": {
      "title": "USD 259 Tech Support",
      "description": "USD 259 Tech Support - Wichita, Kansas, United States USD 259 Tech Support - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode USD 259 Tech Support Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Temporary USD 259 Tech Support 495912 Temporary Department Ennovar Tech Services and Solutions Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $14 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story Ennovar is looking for an employee to work tech support for Wichita Public Schools USD 259. Job Duties Works under the supervision of the Site Technology Specialist (STS). Displays a high skill level and technical expertise relating to computer technology, networking, and other functions of the assignment. Conducts in-service training activities for building personnel regarding the proper use and maintenance of computer equipment and software. Meets specified deadlines and confers with the STS to ensure the satisfactory execution and completion of a specific job. Works cooperatively with others in order to maintain a harmonious and efficient operation. Coordinates with STS and district support organizations on technology issues for the site. Determines priority with the STS. Tracks backlog of requests. Escalates problems as necessary. Performs workstation hardware/software setup and maintenance to include: * Hardware upgrades and installs * OS installs and updates * Software installs and updates * Repair of hardware components, working with the STS for the appropriate warranty replacement work Serves as a resource for troubleshooting technology systems issues (hardware, software, network). Demonstrates understanding of site network topology. Performs network administration. Assists the STS as necessary in managing student and staff user accounts and network shares. Installs and manages server-based applications, as necessary. Performs network troubleshooting of switches and network drops in classrooms/offices, escalating problems if necessary. Performs all other duties as required by the STS. Additional Requirements - Must work a minimum of 25 hours, Monday-Friday, between the hours of 7:30 AM - 4:30 PM. - Must be self-sustaining - Must have basic IT knowledge - Preferred Major(s): MIS, Cybersecurity, Computer Science, Computer Engineering Apply Now First Name (required) 25ff789c Last Name (required) 1d756f36 Email (required) a38e3943 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) cc427ce9 Last Name (required) a2e973bb Email (required) c37e78d6 Job Alert f2b59579 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 3c354467 Last Name (required