    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/tutor-disability-support-services-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Tutor - Disability Support Services",
      "description": "Tutor - Disability Support Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States Tutor - Disability Support Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Tutor - Disability Support Services Strategic Engagement & Planning | Student Tutor - Disability Support Services 499918 Student Department TRIO Disability Support Services Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $12/hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Flexible, dependent on class schedule. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story As a tutor with TRIO Disability Support Services, you will meet weekly with students to help them become self-sufficient, independent learners and assist them in understanding areas and topics in courses with which they are experiencing difficulty. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Make a commitment to be available to tutor for the ENTIRE semester. • Attend all scheduled tutoring sessions on time. • Maintain contact via face-to-face, phone, or email communication with the Tutor Coordinator in the event of any concerns/problems. Keep the Tutor Coordinator aware of any address, telephone, or schedule changes. • Attend the mandatory CRLA Tutor Training at the beginning of the Fall/Spring semesters. • Attend all monthly tutor meetings/trainings. • Conduct all sessions on campus in the TRIO DSS tutoring rooms, Ablah Library, or any other available building on campus. Off campus locations are prohibited. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements 1. Tutor must be currently enrolled at WSU as an undergraduate/graduate student 2. Must be of sophomore or higher class standing 3. A strong academic background in the subjects to be tutored 4. Maintain a minimum overall GPA of 3.0 5. Must have a B or better in the course to be tutored 6. Must have proficient English-speaking skills 7. Transfer students must have completed at least one full semester at WSU Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications 1. Applicants who have taken the course(s) they wish to tutor at Wichita State University 2. Experience tutoring or working with individuals with disabilities Additional Information We would like for applicants to upload their unofficial transcript to verify position qualifications. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) c847f549 Last Name (required) 2f43fc1b Email (required) fd311b07 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ff768286 Last Name (required) 795443ee Email (required) a9da1d13 Job Alert a20faea8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You?