    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/project-specialist-gls-grant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Project Specialist - GLS Grant",
      "description": "Project Specialist - GLS Grant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Project Specialist - GLS Grant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Project Specialist - GLS Grant Student Affairs (College) | Academic/Student Support, Staff Project Specialist - GLS Grant 499881 Academic/Student Support Staff Department: HOPE Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range begins at $22 per hour and can be adjusted based on experience Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8 am - 5 pm; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story At HOPE Services, we believe every student deserves the support they need to thrive. Join our team to oversee a 4-year Garrett Lee Smith campus grant focused on promoting mental wellness and reducing suicide and substance misuse. You'll collaborate with campus and community partners, foster connections, and champion resources that strengthen our campus community. Job Summary Coordinates and/or facilitates assigned prevention project(s), which may include, but is not limited to, support for project timeline and deliverable tracking, team meetings, training, materials preparation, and promotion of services. Essential Functions Monitors project plans, schedules and budgets, including grant coordination. Recommends alternative actions based on tracking outcomes. Coordinates, organizes and supports project promotions to targeted audience, including providing education to related University stakeholders. Documents and tracks project progress metrics compared to goals. Coordinates and prepares reports, promotional materials and presentations to support leaders. Coordinates and/or facilitates project tasks and trainings as assigned. Allocates work assignments and evaluates services of staff and/or volunteers. Maintains relationships with internal and/or external partners related to specific prevention service area(s). Remains current on related trends and research literature. Job Duties Responsibilities include planning projects, tracking budgets, tracking project goals, creating and maintaining relationships with internal and external partners, overseeing student workers, creating and advertising resources, and engaging the community in trainings, events, and awareness campaigns. The selected individual will also engage in professional development in order to ensure best practices are utilized as well as work with the grant organization to ensure grant goals are appropriately executed and reported. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree in social sciences, public health, communications or related field One (1) year of experience in mental health in higher education or related field. Every 15 hours of graduate college coursework can be substituted for one (1) year of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of best practices regarding promoting mental health, preventing suicide, and preventing substance misuse. Ability to manage multiple assignments simultaneously. Attention to detail. Ability to engage others in shared goals and programming. Ability to execute awareness campaigns. Strong ability to adapt training curriculum and provide public trainings. Ability to manage a budget. Ability to work collaboratively in a professional office environment. Excellent computer and interpersonal skills. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Light Work: Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force to constantly move objects. Light work involves remaining stationary most of the time. Apply Now First Name (required) 4ffc136f Last Name (required) 9cc7cf36 Email (required) 59766375 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6f00d63d Last Name (required) 1438613d Email (required) b25c8787 Job Alert dbcfbfb0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic/Student Support Staff Academic/Student Support Staff Department(s) Student Affairs (College) Student Affairs (College) Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 630d7aec Last Name (required) bbc6d6da Email (required) 60fca618 Send This Job To: 2e5d807d Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, e